The agent edition has `game.settings`, `game.fullscreen`, the corner, the pausing and `input.label`, but not the menu screens: its corner's menu button pauses and resumes.\n\nWhat stays your game's job, because only the game knows it:\n- Every gameplay scene `pausable: true`, so the menu and the pausing reach it; titles and game overs not.\n- Prompts from `game.input.label(action)` (or `ui.hud({ prompt: { act: 'interact' } })`), never hard-coded keys; touch buttons (`touch: [...]`) for every action a level needs (the stick moves).\n- The assists your mechanics call for, as settings: difficulty, aim assist, auto-fire, hold or toggle for a sustained action, hints after repeated failure.\n- Saves: `game.saves` (three slots and an autosave with their place, level and time played; versioned; `menu: { saves: true }` for the pause menu's Save and Load and the standard screen, which asks before a save is lost), written at checkpoints and save points (not on page close).\n- Information never in color alone; flashes short (`game.flash` already follows the settings).\n\n## Frame order\n\n`game.start(...)` runs this every animation frame:\n\n1. The clock adds the frame's real time (at most 50 ms) to what is left from the last frame, and runs one step for each whole 1/120 s of it: 2 steps a frame at 60 Hz, 1 at 120 Hz, 1 or 0 at 144 Hz. Each step ticks input, then (except during hit-stop and pause) runs the timers, the current scene's `update(dt)`, particles and the camera. The rest waits for the next frame: `game.alpha` (0..1) is how much of a step it holds, for interpolating drawing.\n   - Slow motion (`game.timeScale = .3`) makes each step shorter (`dt = 1/120 * .3`), never fewer, so it stays smooth. Above 1 a step is split so none is longer than 1/120 s.\n   - Paused, or at `timeScale` 0, the steps still run with `dt` 0, so input keeps ticking.\n2. The renderer clears the buffer and positions the camera.\n3. The scene's `draw(r)`. Draw backgrounds first, then register decals, queue items, actors, sprites, overlays and lights.\n4. The renderer finishes the frame, in this order:\n   1. particles and afterimages are queued;\n   2. decals draw (ground marks, shadows, telegraphs);\n   3. the queue sorts and draws by depth;\n   4. lighting darkens the frame;\n   5. overlays draw on top (HUD, dialog, menus, damage numbers);\n   6. the frame is presented with a sub-pixel camera offset.\n5. With GPU lighting active, every queue item is also drawn into a hidden info image, and WebGPU does the lighting and presentation.\n\nAn error in `update` or `draw` does not stop the loop. It is shown in a red box on screen and logged once to the console (`game.errors` keeps the list).\n\n## Systems in more depth\n### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n- `E.sees(guard, hero, { map, range: 120, fov: 1.6, eye })` → `{ seen, d, angle, exposure }`: inside the cone, and three points on the hero (feet, chest, head) checked against every top with `map.ray`. Crouching shows less and lower; `hero.exposure` (0..1) is cover you set: tall grass, shadow.\n- `E.hears(guard, { x, y, z, loud: 80 }, map)`: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius, halved through a wall.\n- `const mind = new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget })`; each step `mind.update(dt, E.sees(...), hero)` → `'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'` (it rises faster the nearer and more exposed the hero is), `mind.last` (where it last saw or heard), `mind.changed`. An alert guard that loses the hero searches for `forget` seconds; `mind.hear(strength, at)` notices a noise.\n- Drawing: `r.sightCone(guard, { map, range, fov, color, alpha })` (cut short by walls) and `r.marker(x, y, z, { label, color })`, an objective marker that becomes an arrow at the screen's edge.\n\n### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\nA modern adaptation (Assassin's Creed, Breath of the Wild) wants readable HTML screens over the pixel world, not pixel windows. `E.Shell` builds them from data, so you write none of the HTML, CSS or focus handling. It shows the game's state and holds none of it: you pass values in each step and callbacks for the buttons. The STEALTH slice (`src/starter/70-stealth.js`: the objective, health, status, the takedown prompt, toasts, the results) and the template game use it; copy from them.\n- `const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont }, settings: { items: [{ key: 'cones', label: 'Sight cones', value: true }], onChange(s, key) {} }, screens: { pause: {...}, help: {...} } })`. It takes over from the engine's own and keeps the standard menu (see Standard features). Your items join `game.settings` (`ui.settings` is the same object), saved and checked with the rest; `onChange` hears every change.\n- Screens: `ui.show(name, spec)`, `ui.back()`, `ui.hide()`, `ui.screen` (the open one's name, or null). Every spec takes `kicker`, `title`, `text` (strings or functions), `actions: [[label, fn], { label, act, primary, disabled }]` (falsy entries are skipped, so `cond && [...]` works; `act` taps an input action) and `back`. Then: `'title'` (`name`, `subtitle`, `meta`, `footer`), `'pause'` (Resume first, then your actions, then Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help and Quit to title; it opens while `game.paused` and Resume unpauses; `screens: { pause: false }` leaves it out), `'settings'`, `'controls'`, `'help'` (`keys: [[key, what]]`, `sections: [[heading, text]]`), `'results'` (`emblem`, `stats: [[value, label]]`, `medals: [[label, earned]]`) and `'map'` (`map`, `at`, `markers`, `labels`, `onPick(x, y)` for a waypoint). A screen opened from another stacks; cancel goes back.\n- The HUD, each step: `ui.hud({ objective: { step, title, text, at, from }, status, bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'pips' | 'bar', color }], counts: [[label, value]], prompt: { key, label, hint, progress }, tip, place, keys, buttons: [[label, fn]], minimap: { map, at, markers, onClick } })`. A piece left out is hidden, only what changed is redrawn, and the HUD hides while a screen is open. `objective` shows the distance in meters (`meters: .125` a world unit) and whether the target is above or below. `ui.toast(title, text, seconds)` and `ui.tutorial(title, text, seconds)` come and go on their own.\n- Input: the game's own input moves the focus (keys, d-pad, stick: up / down / left / right, a slider or a choice turns left and right), confirm presses, cancel goes back, pause closes the menu; touch taps. While a screen is open the game's actions are held back, so a menu press doesn't also attack. Touch players reach the menu with the touch START or the corner's button; `buttons: [['Map', openMap]]` adds your own.\n- It honors reduced motion and the safe-area insets, is headless-safe (it keeps its screens' names and draws nothing), and `game.dispose()` takes it away.\n\n### Lighting\n- Light every scene (the Look target's step 9): a dark game with no lights reads flat, and a judge says so. Canvas lighting leads because it draws the same in every browser and every headless check: set `lights.enabled` and `ambient` (.4-.6 for dusk and interiors) in the scene's `enter`, then call `lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity, { color })` every frame where light would come from (lamps, torches, windows, the objective's glow). Light is measured on the ground in ground views, and on screen in side views and for PlatformMaps. The template game and the STEALTH slice show it. Its pass costs a few milliseconds a frame at 320x240 (more on a phone): a heavy scene can keep it for a computer, `matchMedia('(pointer: fine)').matches`, as the STEALTH slice does.\n- GPU lighting (`game.enableGPU({ map })`) needs WebGPU and a TileMap. It adds:\n  - colored lights, and soft shadows cast by walls and `lights.caster(...)`;\n  - light that wraps around characters;\n  - glow from `px.glow`, emissive decals and actors, and `[r, g, b, glow]` floor texels;\n  - bloom and heat shimmer (`lights.heat`).\n- Where GPU lighting can't draw (no WebGPU, still loading, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with `lights.ambient` and the same lights: set both ambients (`gpu.ambient = [r, g, b]`, `lights.ambient`) so the two look alike (the ADVENTURE slice does); `gpu.fallback = false` leaves such frames unlit. Tune the settings, not the shaders.\n\n### Errors and warnings\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.1</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n   126 game/game.js\n   417 kits/stealth.js\n   731 kits/adventure.js\n  1274 total","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181322__x8b64cc/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012drDrnViF4WKxeQcK37Vkj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7ymST3Fe5VdRfQHPox","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015xdVjwH4QauwQiR5iGn1Co","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/bb-x8b64cc/engine/dist/handoff && cat game/game.js; cat kits/stealth.js","description":"Read template game and stealth kit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6701,"cache_read_input_tokens":82210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6701,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2","uuid":"0369fdd9-e3b1-41eb-a13a-a290bb15cbcd","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:24:01.574Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7ym48fD6UEMT2UVipQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015xdVjwH4QauwQiR5iGn1Co":{"command":"cd /tmp/bb-x8b64cc/engine/dist/handoff && cat game/game.js; cat kits/stealth.js","description":"Read template game and stealth kit"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015xdVjwH4QauwQiR5iGn1Co","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (45.2KB). Full output saved to: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium--20261102-181322--x8b64cc-work/0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2/tool-results/bmdscsj46.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n// end screens are pixel art.\n// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } } });   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\nconst ROOF = 32;\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['############',\n...\n</persisted-output>\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181322__x8b64cc/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2","uuid":"6ce14cf3-d9ff-42e4-998f-f7a73e0a5cff","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:24:01.592Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n// end screens are pixel art.\n// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } } });   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\nconst ROOF = 32;\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['############',\n         '#..........#',\n         '#.@........#',\n         '#....p.....#',\n         '#......RRR.#',\n         '#......RGR.#',\n         '#..s...RRR.#',\n         '#..........#',\n         '############'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, R: 2, G: { tile: 2, spawn: 'gem' }, p: 3, '@': 'hero', s: 'guard' },\n  types: { 1: { h: 48, top: '#5a5068', side: '#3e3650', cut: true },\n           2: { h: ROOF, top: '#9a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n           3: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n  floorMat: 'cobble'   // a material (E.MATERIALS, or '#hex pattern'): the floor, wall faces and tops, shapes' parts all take them\n});\n// set dressing: shapes (E.SHAPES: objects as data, right in every view), solid where they stand (map.solid: walk into one, land on it)\nconst DRESS = [['barrel', 152, 30, { facing: .5 }], ['barrel', 166, 26, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 22, 120, { facing: .3 }], ['cart', 72, 26, { facing: 0 }]];\nfor (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) map.solid(id, x, y, 0, o);\nconst GEM = E.sprite(['.c.', 'cCc', '.c.'], { c: '#48c8f0', C: '#e8faff' }, 2);\nlet hero, heroRig, guard, guardRig, alert, got, won;\n\nfunction reset() {\n  const h = map.find('hero'), g = map.find('guard');\n  hero = new E.Mover({ x: h.x, y: h.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 24, glide: true, staminaMax: 100 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (the roof, 32 high, is climbed)\n  heroRig = heroRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hood: true, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth: '#3a4a6a', cape: '#2a3a52' } });\n  guard = new E.Body({ x: g.x, y: g.y, r: 5 }); guard.facing = 0; guard.dir = 1;\n  guardRig = guardRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'sword', hat: 'helmet', colors: { cloth: '#8a3a32' } });\n  alert = 0; got = false; won = false;\n}\n\nconst title = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(['#141030', '#3a2a60']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);   // centred on any screen\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'ROOFTOP', r.W / 2, m - 52, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('CLIMB WITH ' + game.input.label('jump') + '  TAKE THE GEM  STAY UNSEEN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 8, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center' });\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start')).toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 38, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nconst play = {\n  pausable: true,\n  enter() { game.follow(hero, { z: 16 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5; },\n  exit() { game.lights.enabled = false; ui.hud({}); },\n  update(dt) {\n    const I = game.input, was = !!(hero.wall || hero.action);\n    hero.update(dt, map, I);   // walks, jumps, climbs: the stick and the jump button, through the view\n    if (!was && (hero.wall || hero.action)) game.audio.sfx('jump');\n    // the guard walks the street and watches ahead: its eyes see over the planter, not through the roof\n    guard.vx = guard.dir * 30; guard.update(dt, map);\n    if (guard.x > 112 || guard.hitWall) guard.dir = -1; else if (guard.x < 40) guard.dir = 1;\n    guard.facing = guard.dir > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI;\n    const sees = map.sight(guard, hero) && E.inArc(guard, guard.facing, hero, 110, .6);\n    alert = sees ? alert + dt : Math.max(0, alert - dt * .5);\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got && E.dist(hero, { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }) < 12) { got = true; game.audio.sfx('coin'); game.flash('#c8f4ff', .15); }\n    if (got && hero.z < 2) { won = true; game.go('end'); }   // back down in the street with it\n    else if (alert > 1.2) { won = false; game.audio.sfx('hurt'); game.go('end'); }\n    // the rigs are posed every step from the bodies' motion; draw only draws them\n    heroRig.update(dt, hero.rigState());\n    guardRig.update(dt, { x: guard.x, y: guard.y, z: guard.z, vx: guard.vx, vy: 0, facing: guard.facing, stance: 'ready' });\n    // the HUD, from this step's state (E.Shell redraws only what changed; the keys hide on a touch screen)\n    ui.hud({ objective: got ? { title: 'Bring it down', text: 'Back to the street with it' } : { title: 'Take the gem', text: hero.wall ? 'Climb: up, and jump to leap' : 'It lies on the roof', at: { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }, from: hero },\n      bars: [{ label: 'Seen', value: Math.min(alert, 1.2), max: 1.2, color: '#ff6040' }, { label: 'Stamina', value: hero.stamina, max: hero.staminaMax, color: hero.exhausted ? '#ff6040' : '#7ad06a' }],\n      keys: [[['up', 'left', 'down', 'right'].map(a => I.label(a)).join(''), 'Move'], [I.label('jump'), 'Jump, climb, glide']] });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);   // (the floor runs on past the map to the screen's edges: map.outside)\n    for (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) r.shape(id, x, y, 0, o);\n    r.prop('lamp', 88, 88, 0, { light: true });   // a street lamp: its glow and a pool of light\n    r.decal(() => r.groundArc(guard.x, guard.y, 6, 110, guard.facing - .6, guard.facing + .6, alert > 0 ? '#ff6040' : '#ffe080', .4));   // its sight cone\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got) { r.sprite(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6 + Math.sin(game.time * 3) * 2, GEM, { glow: .8 }); game.lights.add(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6, 44, .9, { color: '#80d8ff' }); }\n    if (hero.gliding) r.queue(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 40, g => {   // the sail, over the hands the rig holds up\n      const c = Math.cos(hero.facing), s = Math.sin(hero.facing), P = (f, w, z) => r.w(hero.x + c * f - s * w, hero.y + s * f + c * w, hero.z + z);\n      const q = [P(9, -17, 43), P(9, 17, 43), P(-7, 15, 37), P(-7, -15, 37)], h = P(0, 0, 30);\n      for (const t of [q[0], q[1]]) E.px.line(g, t[0], t[1], h[0], h[1], '#3a2a20');\n      E.px.poly(g, q, '#d8603a'); E.px.line(g, q[0][0], q[0][1], q[1][0], q[1][1], '#f4a070');\n    });\n    for (const [b, rig] of [[hero, heroRig], [guard, guardRig]]) {\n      r.shadow(b.x, b.y, 7, .35, undefined, b.groundZ || 0);\n      r.actor(b.x, b.y, b.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst end = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(won ? ['#103020', '#2a6a48'] : ['#301010', '#6a2a2a']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, won ? 'STOLEN' : 'CAUGHT', r.W / 2, m - 42, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start') + ' TO TRY AGAIN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 28, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nreset();\n// a handle for tests and tools (node game/test.mjs, tools/check.mjs prints snapshot(), tools/replay.mjs logs it)\ngame.debug = {\n  snapshot: () => ({ scene: game.sceneName, hero: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z].map(v => Math.round(v * 10) / 10), climbing: !!(hero.wall || hero.action),\n    guard: [Math.round(guard.x), Math.round(guard.y), guard.facing], alert: Math.round(alert * 100) / 100, got, won }),\n  teleport(x, y, z = 0, facing = hero.facing) { Object.assign(hero, { x, y, z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, onGround: true, facing, wall: null, action: null }); }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { title, play, end }, scene: 'title' });\n})();\n// The STEALTH kit's game (third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/70-stealth.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. stealth.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs stealth runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\nconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {};\nlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\nconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n];\n/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\nconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n});\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\nconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\nconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\nconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n];\nHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\nconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\nconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\nconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n  try {\n    if (fresh) fresh();\n    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n    return h >>> 0;\n  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n};\n// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\nconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\nconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n    const t = game.time;\n    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n    });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n    titleBg.draw(r);\n    stage.draw(r);\n    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\nconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\nscenes.over = {\n  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 7  STEALTH  (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu). A rooftop district at dusk: steal the ledger from the brick\n * roof and slip out by the east gate. Three guards (one on a roof) patrol with sight cones; what they see makes them\n * notice (?), search the last place they saw you, and at last chase (!) across the roofs. Hide in tall grass while\n * crouched, take a guard down silently from behind (J), or from a roof above (J as you stand over them). In a fight their\n * swings are telegraphed: K just before the blow parries and stuns them.\n * Keys (E.Input.THIRDPERSON): WASD move, Shift sprint, Space jump, climb a wall, vault, leap a gap, C crouch, J attack or\n * take down, K block or parry, L dodge roll, V view. The ledger is a checkpoint. The hero climbs any wall: Space at a\n * face latches on, the stick climbs (up the screen is up the wall), Space leaps up, C lets go. TOUCH: the stick, JUMP,\n * ATTACK, BLOCK, CROUCH.\n * HOW IT WORKS: the hero and the guards are E.Mover bodies (the same climbing, vaulting and gap-leaping for both); a\n * guard's eyes are E.sees through the map's heights, its mind an E.Suspicion, its legs a FlowField that climbs, drops and\n * jumps. Climbs, vaults, rolls and takedowns are E.ACTIONS; the facades are wall-type options; the belfry's canopy sorts by\n * its footprint; r.sightCone and r.marker draw the cones and the objective. Dusk is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n * ambient and the lights added each draw (street lamps, the ledger's glow, the gate), on a computer: its pass costs a\n * few milliseconds a frame, so a phone keeps its frame rate and an unlit street.\n * The interface is HTML, E.Shell's: the objective with its distance, health, status, the takedown prompt, toasts and\n * the results; the guards' marks stay in the world. The music is one song in layers (game.audio.layer): it sneaks on\n * three tracks, and a guard's alert brings in the chase's drums and its saw over them, taken out again when they lose\n * you: no cut to another song.\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst STEALTH = (() => {\n  const T = 16, HP = 3;\n  // SHADOWS ON THE ROOFS: the sneaking bass, ticks and lead; 'chase' and 'alarm' start silent (on: false)\n  const SONG = { bpm: 108, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: .28, notes: 'A2 . . A2 . . A2 . | A2 . . A2 . C3 . . | F2 . . F2 . . F2 . | G2 . . G2 . E2 . .' },\n    { name: 'tick', wave: 'drums', vol: .06, notes: 'h . . h . . h . h . . h . . h .' },\n    { name: 'lead', wave: 'pulse12', vol: .07, notes: 'E5 - . . . . D5 . | C5 - . . B4 . A4 . | . . . . F5 - E5 . | D5 - . . E5 - . . | E5 - . . . . G5 . | F5 - . . E5 . D5 . | C5 - . . D5 - . . | B4 - - - . . . .' },\n    { name: 'chase', wave: 'drums', vol: .13, on: false, notes: 'k . h k s . h . k k h . s . h s' },\n    { name: 'alarm', wave: 'saw', vol: .06, on: false, notes: 'A3 A3 A4 A3 E4 A3 G4 A3 | A3 A3 A4 A3 C5 A3 B4 A3 | F3 F3 F4 F3 C4 F3 E4 F3 | G3 G3 G4 G3 D4 G3 B3 G3' }] };\n  const PAVE = { stones: ['#7a6a60', '#726258', '#806e64'].map(E.hex), mortar: E.hex('#3e3236'), hi: E.hex('#8e7e72'), lo: E.hex('#56484a'), speck: E.hex('#66564e') };   // warm cobbles against the cool stone walls\n  /* ---- THE DISTRICT: roofs 24-56 high a jump apart (3-4 cells), a belfry, tall grass (,) and a planter (p) ---- */\n  const map = new E.TileMap({ rows: [\n    '############################',\n    '#.......................,,,#',\n    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC...,,#',\n    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC.....#',\n    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC..TT.#',\n    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC..TT.#',\n    '#.........................,#',\n    '#..,,,.......p.......,,,..,#',\n    '#..,,,...............,,,...#',\n    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF.......#',\n    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF..GGG..#',\n    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF..GGG..#',\n    '#.@.......................X#',\n    '############################'],\n    legend: { '#': 1, A: 2, B: 3, C: 4, D: 5, E: 6, F: 7, G: 8, T: 9, p: 10, ',': { floor: 'grass' }, '@': 'hero', X: 'exit' },\n    types: {\n      1: { h: 64, top: '#3a3448', side: '#5a5068', face: 'stone', roof: 'plain', cut: true, cutH: 6 },   // the city wall drops low on the camera's side\n      2: { h: 40, top: '#8a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', windows: { lit: .3 }, shutters: '#2a5a8a', door: { chance: .4 } },\n      3: { h: 48, top: '#5a4a3a', side: '#9a6a4a', face: 'brick', roof: 'slab', windows: { lit: .2 }, balcony: { z: 30, color: '#3a2a1e' } },\n      4: { h: 40, top: '#4a6a3a', side: '#b8a888', face: 'timber', roof: 'tiles', arch: { chance: .5 }, windows: true },\n      5: { h: 24, top: '#7a4a32', side: '#d0c0a0', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', door: { chance: .5, color: '#5a2a1a' }, windows: { from: 12, lit: .4 } },\n      6: { h: 48, top: '#6a5a6a', side: '#7a7a8a', face: 'stone', roof: 'plain', windows: { w: 4, h: 12, lit: .15 } },\n      7: { h: 40, top: '#8a5a3a', side: '#c8a888', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', windows: true, shutters: '#6a3a2a', balcony: { z: 24 } },\n      8: { h: 24, top: '#4a6a3a', side: '#a89878', face: 'timber', roof: 'tiles', arch: { chance: .6 } },\n      9: { h: 72, top: '#7a6a5a', side: '#a89878', face: 'sandstone', roof: 'plain', windows: { w: 3, h: 10, step: 22, lit: .5 } },   // the belfry: face, a MATERIAL (docs/ASSETS.md)\n      10: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n    floorTex: (x, y, tag) => tag === 'grass' ? E.tex.grass(x, y, { base: '#3e6a32', dark: '#2a5226', light: '#5a8a42' }) : E.tex.flagstone(x, y, PAVE)\n  });\n  const LEDGER = { x: 11.5 * T, y: 3.5 * T, z: 48 }, EXIT = map.find('exit'), GRASS = [];\n  // set dressing: SHAPES (E.SHAPES, docs/ASSETS.md: objects as data, right in every view) along the north street, out of the patrols' way\n  const DRESS = [['barrel', 1.5 * T, 1.4 * T, { facing: .4 }], ['barrel', 2.5 * T, 1.3 * T, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 7.4 * T, 1.4 * T, { scale: .8, facing: .2 }],\n    ['cart', 15.5 * T, 1.5 * T, { facing: 0 }], ['sack', 16.9 * T, 1.3 * T, { facing: 1 }], ['barrel', 22.6 * T, 1.4 * T, { facing: 3 }],\n    // stacked planks from the asset store, cut into the page's 'stealth' set (src/assets/sets/stealth.js; none without it)\n    ...(E.addAssets((window.ASSETS || {}).stealth || { set: 'stealth' }).shapes.length ? [['stealth:resource-planks', 12.2 * T, 1.4 * T, { scale: .7, facing: Math.PI / 2 + .1 }]] : [])];\n  for (let cy = 0; cy < map.h; cy++) for (let cx = 0; cx < map.w; cx++) if (map.floorAt((cx + .5) * T, (cy + .5) * T) === 'grass') GRASS.push([(c","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181322__x8b64cc/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium--20261102-181322--x8b64cc-work/0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2/tool-results/bmdscsj46.txt","persistedOutputSize":46248},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015xdVjwH4QauwQiR5iGn1Co","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7yzPZgpt6D7BGh1MJT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M9WRwADHciorWc91jBiLrx","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium--20261102-181322--x8b64cc-work/0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2/tool-results/bmdscsj46.txt","allow_large":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1087,"cache_read_input_tokens":88911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1087,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2","uuid":"10a93edf-896c-4d0e-b6e2-52faa009e4ab","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:24:04.763Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7yz1zaFhLzQ11eT4YC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01M9WRwADHciorWc91jBiLrx":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium--20261102-181322--x8b64cc-work/0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2/tool-results/bmdscsj46.txt","allow_large":true}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M9WRwADHciorWc91jBiLrx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n2\t// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n3\t// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n4\t// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n5\t// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n6\t// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n7\t// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n8\t// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n9\t// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n10\t// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n11\t// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n12\t// end screens are pixel art.\n13\t// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n14\t(() => {\n15\tconst E = My3D2dge;\n16\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n17\t  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } } });   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\n18\tconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\n19\tconst ROOF = 32;\n20\tconst map = new E.TileMap({\n21\t  rows: ['############',\n22\t         '#..........#',\n23\t         '#.@........#',\n24\t         '#....p.....#',\n25\t         '#......RRR.#',\n26\t         '#......RGR.#',\n27\t         '#..s...RRR.#',\n28\t         '#..........#',\n29\t         '############'],\n30\t  legend: { '#': 1, R: 2, G: { tile: 2, spawn: 'gem' }, p: 3, '@': 'hero', s: 'guard' },\n31\t  types: { 1: { h: 48, top: '#5a5068', side: '#3e3650', cut: true },\n32\t           2: { h: ROOF, top: '#9a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n33\t           3: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n34\t  floorMat: 'cobble'   // a material (E.MATERIALS, or '#hex pattern'): the floor, wall faces and tops, shapes' parts all take them\n35\t});\n36\t// set dressing: shapes (E.SHAPES: objects as data, right in every view), solid where they stand (map.solid: walk into one, land on it)\n37\tconst DRESS = [['barrel', 152, 30, { facing: .5 }], ['barrel', 166, 26, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 22, 120, { facing: .3 }], ['cart', 72, 26, { facing: 0 }]];\n38\tfor (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) map.solid(id, x, y, 0, o);\n39\tconst GEM = E.sprite(['.c.', 'cCc', '.c.'], { c: '#48c8f0', C: '#e8faff' }, 2);\n40\tlet hero, heroRig, guard, guardRig, alert, got, won;\n41\t\n42\tfunction reset() {\n43\t  const h = map.find('hero'), g = map.find('guard');\n44\t  hero = new E.Mover({ x: h.x, y: h.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 24, glide: true, staminaMax: 100 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (the roof, 32 high, is climbed)\n45\t  heroRig = heroRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hood: true, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth: '#3a4a6a', cape: '#2a3a52' } });\n46\t  guard = new E.Body({ x: g.x, y: g.y, r: 5 }); guard.facing = 0; guard.dir = 1;\n47\t  guardRig = guardRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'sword', hat: 'helmet', colors: { cloth: '#8a3a32' } });\n48\t  alert = 0; got = false; won = false;\n49\t}\n50\t\n51\tconst title = {\n52\t  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n53\t  draw(r) {\n54\t    r.sky(['#141030', '#3a2a60']);\n55\t    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);   // centred on any screen\n56\t    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'ROOFTOP', r.W / 2, m - 52, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n57\t    r.text(('CLIMB WITH ' + game.input.label('jump') + '  TAKE THE GEM  STAY UNSEEN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 8, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center' });\n58\t    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start')).toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 38, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n59\t  }\n60\t};\n61\t\n62\tconst play = {\n63\t  pausable: true,\n64\t  enter() { game.follow(hero, { z: 16 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5; },\n65\t  exit() { game.lights.enabled = false; ui.hud({}); },\n66\t  update(dt) {\n67\t    const I = game.input, was = !!(hero.wall || hero.action);\n68\t    hero.update(dt, map, I);   // walks, jumps, climbs: the stick and the jump button, through the view\n69\t    if (!was && (hero.wall || hero.action)) game.audio.sfx('jump');\n70\t    // the guard walks the street and watches ahead: its eyes see over the planter, not through the roof\n71\t    guard.vx = guard.dir * 30; guard.update(dt, map);\n72\t    if (guard.x > 112 || guard.hitWall) guard.dir = -1; else if (guard.x < 40) guard.dir = 1;\n73\t    guard.facing = guard.dir > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI;\n74\t    const sees = map.sight(guard, hero) && E.inArc(guard, guard.facing, hero, 110, .6);\n75\t    alert = sees ? alert + dt : Math.max(0, alert - dt * .5);\n76\t    const gem = map.find('gem');\n77\t    if (!got && E.dist(hero, { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }) < 12) { got = true; game.audio.sfx('coin'); game.flash('#c8f4ff', .15); }\n78\t    if (got && hero.z < 2) { won = true; game.go('end'); }   // back down in the street with it\n79\t    else if (alert > 1.2) { won = false; game.audio.sfx('hurt'); game.go('end'); }\n80\t    // the rigs are posed every step from the bodies' motion; draw only draws them\n81\t    heroRig.update(dt, hero.rigState());\n82\t    guardRig.update(dt, { x: guard.x, y: guard.y, z: guard.z, vx: guard.vx, vy: 0, facing: guard.facing, stance: 'ready' });\n83\t    // the HUD, from this step's state (E.Shell redraws only what changed; the keys hide on a touch screen)\n84\t    ui.hud({ objective: got ? { title: 'Bring it down', text: 'Back to the street with it' } : { title: 'Take the gem', text: hero.wall ? 'Climb: up, and jump to leap' : 'It lies on the roof', at: { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }, from: hero },\n85\t      bars: [{ label: 'Seen', value: Math.min(alert, 1.2), max: 1.2, color: '#ff6040' }, { label: 'Stamina', value: hero.stamina, max: hero.staminaMax, color: hero.exhausted ? '#ff6040' : '#7ad06a' }],\n86\t      keys: [[['up', 'left', 'down', 'right'].map(a => I.label(a)).join(''), 'Move'], [I.label('jump'), 'Jump, climb, glide']] });\n87\t  },\n88\t  draw(r) {\n89\t    map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);   // (the floor runs on past the map to the screen's edges: map.outside)\n90\t    for (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) r.shape(id, x, y, 0, o);\n91\t    r.prop('lamp', 88, 88, 0, { light: true });   // a street lamp: its glow and a pool of light\n92\t    r.decal(() => r.groundArc(guard.x, guard.y, 6, 110, guard.facing - .6, guard.facing + .6, alert > 0 ? '#ff6040' : '#ffe080', .4));   // its sight cone\n93\t    const gem = map.find('gem');\n94\t    if (!got) { r.sprite(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6 + Math.sin(game.time * 3) * 2, GEM, { glow: .8 }); game.lights.add(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6, 44, .9, { color: '#80d8ff' }); }\n95\t    if (hero.gliding) r.queue(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 40, g => {   // the sail, over the hands the rig holds up\n96\t      const c = Math.cos(hero.facing), s = Math.sin(hero.facing), P = (f, w, z) => r.w(hero.x + c * f - s * w, hero.y + s * f + c * w, hero.z + z);\n97\t      const q = [P(9, -17, 43), P(9, 17, 43), P(-7, 15, 37), P(-7, -15, 37)], h = P(0, 0, 30);\n98\t      for (const t of [q[0], q[1]]) E.px.line(g, t[0], t[1], h[0], h[1], '#3a2a20');\n99\t      E.px.poly(g, q, '#d8603a'); E.px.line(g, q[0][0], q[0][1], q[1][0], q[1][1], '#f4a070');\n100\t    });\n101\t    for (const [b, rig] of [[hero, heroRig], [guard, guardRig]]) {\n102\t      r.shadow(b.x, b.y, 7, .35, undefined, b.groundZ || 0);\n103\t      r.actor(b.x, b.y, b.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n104\t    }\n105\t  }\n106\t};\n107\t\n108\tconst end = {\n109\t  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n110\t  draw(r) {\n111\t    r.sky(won ? ['#103020', '#2a6a48'] : ['#301010', '#6a2a2a']);\n112\t    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);\n113\t    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, won ? 'STOLEN' : 'CAUGHT', r.W / 2, m - 42, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n114\t    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start') + ' TO TRY AGAIN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 28, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n115\t  }\n116\t};\n117\t\n118\treset();\n119\t// a handle for tests and tools (node game/test.mjs, tools/check.mjs prints snapshot(), tools/replay.mjs logs it)\n120\tgame.debug = {\n121\t  snapshot: () => ({ scene: game.sceneName, hero: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z].map(v => Math.round(v * 10) / 10), climbing: !!(hero.wall || hero.action),\n122\t    guard: [Math.round(guard.x), Math.round(guard.y), guard.facing], alert: Math.round(alert * 100) / 100, got, won }),\n123\t  teleport(x, y, z = 0, facing = hero.facing) { Object.assign(hero, { x, y, z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, onGround: true, facing, wall: null, action: null }); }\n124\t};\n125\tgame.start({ scenes: { title, play, end }, scene: 'title' });\n126\t})();\n127\t// The STEALTH kit's game (third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n128\t// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/70-stealth.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n129\t// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. stealth.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs stealth runs it headless.\n130\t/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n131\t * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n132\t * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n133\t * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n134\t * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n135\t * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n136\t * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n137\t * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n138\t * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n139\t * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n140\t * ======================================================================== */\n141\t(() => {\n142\t'use strict';\n143\tconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n144\t\n145\t/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n146\t * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\n147\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\n148\tconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\n149\tconst scenes = {};\n150\tlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\n151\tconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n152\t// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n153\t// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\n154\tconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n155\t// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\n156\tconst SLICES = [\n157\t  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n158\t  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n159\t  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n160\t  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n161\t  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n162\t  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n163\t  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n164\t  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n165\t  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n166\t  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n167\t  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n168\t  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n169\t  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n170\t  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n171\t  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n172\t  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n173\t  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n174\t  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n175\t  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n176\t  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n177\t  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n178\t  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n179\t];\n180\t/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n181\t   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n182\t   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n183\t   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\n184\tconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\n185\taddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n186\t  if (e.repeat) return;\n187\t  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n188\t  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n189\t  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n190\t  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n191\t  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n192\t});\n193\t\n194\t/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n195\t * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\n196\tconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n197\t  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\n198\tconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\n199\tconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n200\t  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n201\t  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n202\t  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n203\t  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n204\t  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n205\t  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n206\t];\n207\tHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n208\t// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\n209\tconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n210\t// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\n211\tconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n212\t/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n213\t * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n214\t * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n215\t * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n216\t * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\n217\tconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n218\t  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n219\t  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n220\t  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n221\t  try {\n222\t    if (fresh) fresh();\n223\t    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n224\t    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n225\t    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n226\t    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n227\t    return h >>> 0;\n228\t  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n229\t};\n230\t// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\n231\tconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n232\t// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\n233\tconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n234\t/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n235\t *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\n236\tconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\n237\tlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\n238\tscenes.title = {\n239\t  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n240\t  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n241\t  update(dt) {\n242\t    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n243\t    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n244\t    const t = game.time;\n245\t    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n246\t      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n247\t      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n248\t    });\n249\t  },\n250\t  draw(r) {\n251\t    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n252\t    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n253\t    titleBg.draw(r);\n254\t    stage.draw(r);\n255\t    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n256\t    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n257\t    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n258\t    r.overlay(g => {\n259\t      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n260\t      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n261\t      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n262\t    });\n263\t    titleMenu.draw(r);\n264\t    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n265\t      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n266\t    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n267\t  }\n268\t};\n269\t\n270\t/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\n271\tconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\n272\tconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n273\t  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\n274\tscenes.over = {\n275\t  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n276\t  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n277\t  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n278\t  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n279\t  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n280\t    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n281\t    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n282\t  }\n283\t};\n284\t\n285\t/* =====================================================================================\n286\t * SLICE 7  STEALTH  (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu). A rooftop district at dusk: steal the ledger from the brick\n287\t * roof and slip out by the east gate. Three guards (one on a roof) patrol with sight cones; what they see makes them\n288\t * notice (?), search the last place they saw you, and at last chase (!) across the roofs. Hide in tall grass while\n289\t * crouched, take a guard down silently from behind (J), or from a roof above (J as you stand over them). In a fight their\n290\t * swings are telegraphed: K just before the blow parries and stuns them.\n291\t * Keys (E.Input.THIRDPERSON): WASD move, Shift sprint, Space jump, climb a wall, vault, leap a gap, C crouch, J attack or\n292\t * take down, K block or parry, L dodge roll, V view. The ledger is a checkpoint. The hero climbs any wall: Space at a\n293\t * face latches on, the stick climbs (up the screen is up the wall), Space leaps up, C lets go. TOUCH: the stick, JUMP,\n294\t * ATTACK, BLOCK, CROUCH.\n295\t * HOW IT WORKS: the hero and the guards are E.Mover bodies (the same climbing, vaulting and gap-leaping for both); a\n296\t * guard's eyes are E.sees through the map's heights, its mind an E.Suspicion, its legs a FlowField that climbs, drops and\n297\t * jumps. Climbs, vaults, rolls and takedowns are E.ACTIONS; the facades are wall-type options; the belfry's canopy sorts by\n298\t * its footprint; r.sightCone and r.marker draw the cones and the objective. Dusk is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n299\t * ambient and the lights added each draw (street lamps, the ledger's glow, the gate), on a computer: its pass costs a\n300\t * few milliseconds a frame, so a phone keeps its frame rate and an unlit street.\n301\t * The interface is HTML, E.Shell's: the objective with its distance, health, status, the takedown prompt, toasts and\n302\t * the results; the guards' marks stay in the world. The music is one song in layers (game.audio.layer): it sneaks on\n303\t * three tracks, and a guard's alert brings in the chase's drums and its saw over them, taken out again when they lose\n304\t * you: no cut to another song.\n305\t * ===================================================================================== */\n306\tconst STEALTH = (() => {\n307\t  const T = 16, HP = 3;\n308\t  // SHADOWS ON THE ROOFS: the sneaking bass, ticks and lead; 'chase' and 'alarm' start silent (on: false)\n309\t  const SONG = { bpm: 108, steps: 4, tracks: [\n310\t    { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: .28, notes: 'A2 . . A2 . . A2 . | A2 . . A2 . C3 . . | F2 . . F2 . . F2 . | G2 . . G2 . E2 . .' },\n311\t    { name: 'tick', wave: 'drums', vol: .06, notes: 'h . . h . . h . h . . h . . h .' },\n312\t    { name: 'lead', wave: 'pulse12', vol: .07, notes: 'E5 - . . . . D5 . | C5 - . . B4 . A4 . | . . . . F5 - E5 . | D5 - . . E5 - . . | E5 - . . . . G5 . | F5 - . . E5 . D5 . | C5 - . . D5 - . . | B4 - - - . . . .' },\n313\t    { name: 'chase', wave: 'drums', vol: .13, on: false, notes: 'k . h k s . h . k k h . s . h s' },\n314\t    { name: 'alarm', wave: 'saw', vol: .06, on: false, notes: 'A3 A3 A4 A3 E4 A3 G4 A3 | A3 A3 A4 A3 C5 A3 B4 A3 | F3 F3 F4 F3 C4 F3 E4 F3 | G3 G3 G4 G3 D4 G3 B3 G3' }] };\n315\t  const PAVE = { stones: ['#7a6a60', '#726258', '#806e64'].map(E.hex), mortar: E.hex('#3e3236'), hi: E.hex('#8e7e72'), lo: E.hex('#56484a'), speck: E.hex('#66564e') };   // warm cobbles against the cool stone walls\n316\t  /* ---- THE DISTRICT: roofs 24-56 high a jump apart (3-4 cells), a belfry, tall grass (,) and a planter (p) ---- */\n317\t  const map = new E.TileMap({ rows: [\n318\t    '############################',\n319\t    '#.......................,,,#',\n320\t    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC...,,#',\n321\t    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC.....#',\n322\t    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC..TT.#',\n323\t    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC..TT.#',\n324\t    '#.........................,#',\n325\t    '#..,,,.......p.......,,,..,#',\n326\t    '#..,,,...............,,,...#',\n327\t    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF.......#',\n328\t    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF..GGG..#',\n329\t    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF..GGG..#',\n330\t    '#.@.......................X#',\n331\t    '############################'],\n332\t    legend: { '#': 1, A: 2, B: 3, C: 4, D: 5, E: 6, F: 7, G: 8, T: 9, p: 10, ',': { floor: 'grass' }, '@': 'hero', X: 'exit' },\n333\t    types: {\n334\t      1: { h: 64, top: '#3a3448', side: '#5a5068', face: 'stone', roof: 'plain', cut: true, cutH: 6 },   // the city wall drops low on the camera's side\n335\t      2: { h: 40, top: '#8a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', windows: { lit: .3 }, shutters: '#2a5a8a', door: { chance: .4 } },\n336\t      3: { h: 48, top: '#5a4a3a', side: '#9a6a4a', face: 'brick', roof: 'slab', windows: { lit: .2 }, balcony: { z: 30, color: '#3a2a1e' } },\n337\t      4: { h: 40, top: '#4a6a3a', side: '#b8a888', face: 'timber', roof: 'tiles', arch: { chance: .5 }, windows: true },\n338\t      5: { h: 24, top: '#7a4a32', side: '#d0c0a0', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', door: { chance: .5, color: '#5a2a1a' }, windows: { from: 12, lit: .4 } },\n339\t      6: { h: 48, top: '#6a5a6a', side: '#7a7a8a', face: 'stone', roof: 'plain', windows: { w: 4, h: 12, lit: .15 } },\n340\t      7: { h: 40, top: '#8a5a3a', side: '#c8a888', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', windows: true, shutters: '#6a3a2a', balcony: { z: 24 } },\n341\t      8: { h: 24, top: '#4a6a3a', side: '#a89878', face: 'timber', roof: 'tiles', arch: { chance: .6 } },\n342\t      9: { h: 72, top: '#7a6a5a', side: '#a89878', face: 'sandstone', roof: 'plain', windows: { w: 3, h: 10, step: 22, lit: .5 } },   // the belfry: face, a MATERIAL (docs/ASSETS.md)\n343\t      10: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n344\t    floorTex: (x, y, tag) => tag === 'grass' ? E.tex.grass(x, y, { base: '#3e6a32', dark: '#2a5226', light: '#5a8a42' }) : E.tex.flagstone(x, y, PAVE)\n345\t  });\n346\t  const LEDGER = { x: 11.5 * T, y: 3.5 * T, z: 48 }, EXIT = map.find('exit'), GRASS = [];\n347\t  // set dressing: SHAPES (E.SHAPES, docs/ASSETS.md: objects as data, right in every view) along the north street, out of the patrols' way\n348\t  const DRESS = [['barrel', 1.5 * T, 1.4 * T, { facing: .4 }], ['barrel', 2.5 * T, 1.3 * T, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 7.4 * T, 1.4 * T, { scale: .8, facing: .2 }],\n349\t    ['cart', 15.5 * T, 1.5 * T, { facing: 0 }], ['sack', 16.9 * T, 1.3 * T, { facing: 1 }], ['barrel', 22.6 * T, 1.4 * T, { facing: 3 }],\n350\t    // stacked planks from the asset store, cut into the page's 'stealth' set (src/assets/sets/stealth.js; none without it)\n351\t    ...(E.addAssets((window.ASSETS || {}).stealth || { set: 'stealth' }).shapes.length ? [['stealth:resource-planks', 12.2 * T, 1.4 * T, { scale: .7, facing: Math.PI / 2 + .1 }]] : [])];\n352\t  for (let cy = 0; cy < map.h; cy++) for (let cx = 0; cx < map.w; cx++) if (map.floorAt((cx + .5) * T, (cy + .5) * T) === 'grass') GRASS.push([(cx + .5) * T, (cy + .5) * T]);\n353\t  const BOOK = E.sprite(['.bbbb.', 'bBBBBb', 'bBwwBb', 'bBBBBb', '.bbbb.'], { b: '#3a2010', B: '#8a3a20', w: '#f0e0b0' });\n354\t  const ROUTES = [   // [start, ...patrol points] in cells, and the guard's roof height\n355\t    [[19.5, 3.5, 40], [21.5, 3.5, 40], [21.5, 5.5, 40], [18.5, 5.5, 40]],\n356\t    [[6.5, 6.5, 0], [20.5, 6.5, 0], [20.5, 8.5, 0], [6.5, 8.5, 0]],\n357\t    [[11.5, 12.2, 0], [20.5, 12.2, 0], [20.5, 8.2, 0], [11.5, 8.2, 0]]\n358\t  ];\n359\t  let hero, rig, guards, attack, checkpoint, ledger, won, over, hp, hurtT, alertT, ui = null;\n360\t  const say = (title, text) => ui.toast(title, text, 3);\n361\t  const inGrass = b => b.z < 2 && map.floorAt(b.x, b.y) === 'grass';\n362\t\n363\t  /* ---- GUARDS: a Mover with patrol points, eyes, a mind and a flow field that climbs, drops and jumps ---- */\n364\t  function makeGuard(route, i) {\n365\t    const [x, y, z] = route[0];\n366\t    const g = new E.Mover({ x: x * T, y: y * T, z, r: 5, run: 70, walk: 30, climbMax: 56, hopMax: 56 });\n367\t    Object.assign(g, { i, route: route.map(p => [p[0] * T, p[1] * T]), at: 1, mind: new E.Suspicion({ rise: 1.6, decay: .25, forget: 7 }), hp: 2, stun: 0, dead: false,\n368\t      flow: new E.FlowField(map, { climb: 56, drop: 56, jump: 60 }), wait: 0, hit: null, swing: new E.Attack('overhead', { wind: .38, recover: .3, reach: 9 }), bark: 0,\n369\t      rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', hat: 'helmet', armor: true, weapon: 'sword', colors: { cloth: ['#8a3a32', '#6a3a5a', '#7a4a2a'][i], metal: '#c8c8d8' } }) });\n370\t    return g;\n371\t  }\n372\t  function guardUpdate(g, dt) {\n373\t    if (g.dead) return;   // (a takedown moves the body it takes: the hero's action plays it)\n374\t    if (g.stun > 0) { g.stun -= dt; g.update(dt, map, { move: [0, 0] }); return; }\n375\t    const seen = hero && !over ? E.sees(g, hero, { map, range: 110, fov: 1.5 }) : { seen: false, exposure: 0 }, st = g.mind.update(dt, seen, hero);\n376\t    if (g.mind.changed && st === 'alert') { A.sfx('select'); g.bark = 1.2; }\n377\t    let goal = null, speed = 'walk';\n378\t    if (st === 'alert') { goal = hero; speed = 'run'; }\n379\t    else if (st === 'search' && g.mind.last) goal = g.mind.last;\n380\t    else if (st === 'notice') { g.facing = E.approachAng(g.facing, Math.atan2(g.mind.last.y - g.y, g.mind.last.x - g.x), dt * 3); g.update(dt, map, { move: [0, 0] }); return; }\n381\t    else { const p = g.route[g.at]; goal = { x: p[0], y: p[1], z: 0 }; if (Math.hypot(p[0] - g.x, p[1] - g.y) < 8) { g.at = (g.at + 1) % g.route.length; g.wait = .8; } }\n382\t    if (g.wait > 0 && st === 'calm') { g.wait -= dt; g.update(dt, map, { move: [0, 0] }); return; }\n383\t    // in reach of the hero: a telegraphed swing (a long wind-up), else walk the field toward the goal\n384\t    const d = Math.hypot(hero.x - g.x, hero.y - g.y), near = st === 'alert' && d < 20 && E.sameLevel(g, hero, 10);\n385\t    if (near && !g.swing.busy && !hero.action) { g.facing = Math.atan2(hero.y - g.y, hero.x - g.x); g.swing.start(); A.sfx('swing', { vol: .5 }); }\n386\t    const began = g.swing.update(dt);\n387\t    if (g.swing.busy) { g.update(dt, map, { move: [0, 0] }); if (g.swing.active && began === 'active') strikeHero(g); return; }\n388\t    let move = [0, 0], jump = false;\n389\t    if (goal) {\n390\t      g.flow.update(goal.x, goal.y);\n391\t      const nx = g.flow.next(g.x, g.y), tx = nx ? nx.x : goal.x, ty = nx ? nx.y : goal.y, l = Math.hypot(tx - g.x, ty - g.y) || 1;\n392\t      if (Math.hypot(goal.x - g.x, goal.y - g.y) > 6) move = [(tx - g.x) / l, (ty - g.y) / l];\n393\t      if (nx && g.onGround && (nx.kind === 'climb' || nx.kind === 'jump') && nx.edge < g.r + 4) { jump = true; g.facing = Math.atan2(ty - g.y, tx - g.x); }\n394\t    }\n395\t    if (speed === 'walk') move = move.map(v => v * .5);\n396\t    g.update(dt, map, { move, sprint: false, jumpPressed: jump });\n397\t  }\n398\t  function strikeHero(g) {\n399\t    if (!E.inArc(g, g.facing, hero, 20, 1.2, 10) || (hero.action && hero.action.invulnerable)) return;\n400\t    if (game.input.down('block') && !hero.action) { A.sfx('hit', { vol: .4 }); P.sparks(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 16, 6, g.facing + Math.PI); return; }\n401\t    hp--; hurtT = .4; game.hitFx(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 16, { power: 1, angle: g.facing, sound: 'hurt' }); E.knockback(g, hero, 140);\n402\t    if (hp <= 0) lose();\n403\t  }\n404\t\n405\t  /* ---- THE HERO: a Mover, a hidden blade, a parry, two takedowns ---- */\n406\t  function start() {\n407\t    const s = map.find('hero');\n408\t    hero = new E.Mover({ x: s.x, y: s.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 30 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (walls up to 30 are pulled up at once, higher ones climbed)\n409\t    rig = rig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', hood: true, weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 7, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.4 }, colors: { cloth: '#d8d2c4', coat: '#d8d2c4', cape: '#8a2a2a', capeIn: '#5a1a1a', pants: '#3a3448', metal: '#e8e8f0' } });\n410\t    attack = new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }); guards = ROUTES.map(makeGuard);\n411\t    ui = ui || new E.Shell(game, { theme: { accent: '#e8c070' } });   // (made once: it takes over from the engine's own, keeping the pause menu)\n412\t    checkpoint = null; ledger = false; won = false; over = false; hp = HP; hurtT = 0; alertT = 0; say('Steal the ledger', 'It lies on the brick roof');\n413\t    game.follow(hero, { z: 18 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.cam.offset = [0, -10]; L.enabled = !!(window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(pointer: fine)').matches); L.ambient = .6; A.music(SONG); A.layer('chase', 0, .02); A.layer('alarm', 0, .02);\n414\t  }\n415\t  function respawnAt(cp) {\n416\t    Object.assign(hero, { x: cp.x, y: cp.y, z: cp.z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, onGround: true, action: null }); hp = HP;\n417\t    guards.forEach((g, i) => { if (!g.dead) { const [x, y, z] = ROUTES[i][0]; Object.assign(g, { x: x * T, y: y * T, z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, at: 1, stun: 0, action: null }); g.mind.reset(); g.swing.cancel(); } });\n418\t    game.cam.snap = true; say('Back at the checkpoint');\n419\t  }\n420\t  function lose() { if (checkpoint) { A.sfx('die'); respawnAt(checkpoint); } else { over = true; game.after(.8, () => game.go('over', { from: 'stealth' })); } }\n421\t  // a takedown within reach: [guard, from above] or null\n422\t  function takedown() {\n423\t    for (const g of guards) {\n424\t      if (g.dead || g.action) continue;\n425\t      const dz = hero.z - g.z, d = Math.hypot(g.x - hero.x, g.y - hero.y);\n426\t      // from above: the hero stands over a guard below, close enough to drop onto them\n427\t      if (dz > 14 && d < 44 && hero.onGround) return [g, true];\n428\t      // from behind: close, on the same level, outside the guard's view and not yet hunting\n429\t      const behind = Math.abs(E.angDiff(g.facing, Math.atan2(g.y - hero.y, g.x - hero.x))) < 1.1;\n430\t      if (E.sameLevel(hero, g) && d < 18 && behind && g.mind.state !== 'alert') return [g, false];\n431\t    }\n432\t    return null;\n433\t  }\n434\t  function tryTakedown() { const t = takedown(); if (!t) return false; hero.play('takedown', { other: t[0], aerial: t[1], map }); return finishGuard(t[0], hero.action); }\n435\t  const parrying = () => guards.some(g => !g.dead && g.swing.phase === 'wind' && g.swing.u > .35 && Math.hypot(g.x - hero.x, g.y - hero.y) < 26);\n436\t  function finishGuard(g, act) { g.dead = true; g.action = act; A.sfx('punch'); game.freeze(.06); return true; }\n437\t  function heroUpdate(dt) {\n438\t    const I = game.input;\n439\t    hero.exposure = inGrass(hero) && hero.crouch ? 0 : 1;   // crouched in tall grass: unseen\n440\t    if (!hero.action) {\n441\t      if (I.pressed('dodge') && hero.dodge(undefined, 34)) A.sfx('whoosh');\n442\t      else if (I.pressed('attack') && !tryTakedown() && attack.start()) { I.consume('attack'); A.sfx('swing'); }\n443\t    }\n444\t    attack.update(dt);\n445\t    attack.hits(guards.filter(g => !g.dead), g => E.inArc(hero, hero.facing, g, 20, 1.3, 10), g => {\n446\t      game.hitFx(g.x, g.y, g.z + 16, { power: g.stun > 0 ? 2 : 1, angle: hero.facing }); E.knockback(hero, g, 90);\n447\t      if (g.stun > 0 || --g.hp <= 0) { g.dead = true; g.action = null; A.sfx('die', { vol: .5 }); } else g.mind.level = 1.2;\n448\t    });\n449\t    // a parry: block in the last moments of a guard's wind-up\n450\t    // CONTEXT touch buttons: ATTACK says TAKE DOWN when one is in reach, BLOCK says PARRY in a guard's wind-up\n451\t    I.touchSet('attack', !hero.action && takedown() ? 'TAKE DOWN' : null); I.touchSet('block', parrying() ? 'PARRY' : null);\n452\t    if (I.pressed('block')) for (const g of guards) if (!g.dead && g.swing.phase === 'wind' && g.swing.u > .35 && Math.hypot(g.x - hero.x, g.y - hero.y) < 26) {\n453\t      g.swing.cancel(); g.stun = 1.3; A.sfx('kick'); game.flash('#ffffff', .08); P.sparks(g.x, g.y, g.z + 18, 10, hero.facing); say('Parried');\n454\t    }\n455\t    hero.update(dt, map, attack.busy ? { move: [0, 0] } : I);\n456\t    if (hero.hurt) { hp--; hurtT = .4; game.shake(3); if (hp <= 0) lose(); }\n457\t    if (hero.inHazard) hero.respawn();\n458\t    if (!ledger && E.dist(hero, LEDGER) < 12) { ledger = true; checkpoint = { x: hero.x, y: hero.y, z: hero.z }; A.sfx('powerup'); say('Checkpoint', 'The ledger is yours: now the east gate'); }\n459\t    if (ledger && !won && Math.hypot(hero.x - EXIT.x, hero.y - EXIT.y) < 14 && hero.z < 2) { won = true; A.music('victory'); results(); }\n460\t  }\n461\t\n462\t  function results() {\n463\t    const alive = guards.filter(g => !g.dead).length, top = best('stealth', alive);\n464\t    ui.show('results', { kicker: 'Mission complete', title: 'The ledger is out', stats: [[String(alive), 'guards who never fell'], [String(top), 'the best yet'], [String(HP - hp), 'wounds taken']],\n465\t      actions: [{ label: 'Back to the title', primary: true, fn: () => { ui.hide(); game.go('title'); } }] });\n466\t  }\n467\t  // the HUD, from this step's state: E.Shell redraws only what changed (keys hide by themselves on a touch screen)\n468\t  function hud() {\n469\t    const k = a => game.input.label(a).toUpperCase(), pad = game.input.lastDevice === 'gamepad', td = !hero.action && takedown();\n470\t    ui.hud(won || over ? {} : {\n471\t      objective: ledger ? { step: '02 / 02', title: 'Slip out by the east gate', text: 'Down in the street, at the far end', at: { x: EXIT.x, y: EXIT.y, z: 0 }, from: hero }\n472\t        : { step: '01 / 02', title: 'Steal the ledger', text: 'On the brick roof', at: LEDGER, from: hero },\n473\t      status: hero.exposure === 0 ? { text: 'Hidden', color: '#9ae89a' } : alertT > 0 ? { text: 'Hunted', color: '#ff4a3a' } : hero.crouch ? 'Crouched' : null,\n474\t      bars: [{ label: 'Health', value: hp, max: HP, kind: 'pips', color: '#e8505a' }], counts: [['Guards down', guards.filter(g => g.dead).length]],\n475\t      prompt: touch() ? null : td ? { act: 'attack', label: 'Take down', hint: td[1] ? 'From above' : 'From behind' } : parrying() ? { act: 'block', label: 'Parry' } : null,\n476\t      keys: [[pad ? 'STICK' : ['up', 'left', 'down', 'right'].map(k).join(''), 'Move'], [k('sprint'), 'Sprint'], [k('jump'), 'Jump, climb'], [k('crouch'), 'Crouch'], [k('attack'), 'Strike'], [k('block'), 'Block'], [k('dodge'), 'Roll']]\n477\t    });\n478\t  }\n479\t\n480\t  function update(dt) {\n481\t    if (hurtT > 0) hurtT -= dt;\n482\t    if (won || over) { hud(); rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ pose: won ? 'cheer' : null })); return; }\n483\t    heroUpdate(dt);\n484\t    for (const g of guards) guardUpdate(g, dt);\n485\t    const alert = guards.some(g => !g.dead && g.mind.state === 'alert');\n486\t    if (alert !== alertT > 0) { alertT = alert ? 1 : 0; A.layer('chase', alert ? 1 : 0, alert ? .4 : 2.5); A.layer('alarm', alert ? 1 : 0, alert ? .8 : 2.5); }   // (the chase comes in by layers, and fades out)\n487\t    rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack: attack.state, pose: game.input.down('block') && !hero.action ? 'block' : null, hurt: hurtT > 0 }));\n488\t    for (const g of guards) {\n489\t      if (g.dead) { g.rig.update(dt, g.action && g.action.other === g ? g.action.otherState() : { x: g.x, y: g.y, z: g.z, facing: g.facing, down: 1 }); continue; }\n490\t      g.rig.update(dt, g.rigState({ attack: g.swing.state, stance: g.mind.state === 'alert' ? 'ready' : null, hurt: g.stun > 0 }));\n491\t      if (g.bark > 0) g.bark -= dt;\n492\t    }\n493\t    hud();\n494\t  }\n495\t\n496\t  const MOOD = { calm: '#ffe080', notice: '#ffc040', search: '#ff9a40', alert: '#ff4a3a' };\n497\t  const LAMPS = [[8.5, 6.2], [16, 8.8], [23.5, 6.2], [12.5, 10.5], [19.5, 1.3]].map(([x, y]) => [x * T, y * T]);   // street lamps, clear of the patrols\n498\t  function draw(r) {\n499\t    map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);   // (the street runs on past the walls to the screen's edges: map.outside)\n500\t    for (const [x, y] of GRASS) r.prop('grass', x, y, 0, { size: 1.3 });\n501\t    for (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) r.shape(id, x, y, 0, o);\n502\t    for (const [x, y] of LAMPS) r.prop('lamp', x, y, 0, { light: true });   // each glows and lights the street (game.lights)\n503\t    if (!ledger) L.add(LEDGER.x, LEDGER.y, LEDGER.z + 6, 40, .8, { color: '#ffd060' }); else L.add(EXIT.x, EXIT.y, 12, 56, .9, { color: '#80e0ff' });\n504\t    // the belfry: a canopy wider than the tower, sorted by its whole footprint (over every tower block)\n505\t    const bx = 25 * T, by = 5 * T, w = 21, H = 20, z = 72;\n506\t    r.queue(bx, by, z, g => { const P2 = (x, y, zz) => r.w(x, y, zz), c = [P2(bx - w, by - w, z), P2(bx + w, by - w, z), P2(bx + w, by + w, z), P2(bx - w, by + w, z)], tip = P2(bx, by, z + H);\n507\t      for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) px.poly(g, [c[i], c[(i + 1) % 4], tip], ['#7a3a2a', '#9a4a32', '#6a2a22', '#8a4232'][i]);\n508\t      px.line(g, tip[0], tip[1], tip[0], tip[1] - 6, '#e8c860'); }, { footprint: [bx - w, by - w, bx + w, by + w] });\n509\t    for (const g of guards) if (!g.dead) r.sightCone(g, { map, range: 110, fov: 1.5, color: MOOD[g.mind.state], alpha: g.mind.state === 'calm' ? .22 : .38 });\n510\t    if (!ledger) r.sprite(LEDGER.x, LEDGER.y, LEDGER.z + 4 + Math.sin(game.time * 3) * 1.5, BOOK, { glow: .6 });\n511\t    const shadow = b => r.shadow(b.x, b.y, 6, .35, undefined, map.groundAt(b.x, b.y, b.r, b.z));\n512\t    shadow(hero); r.actor(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view), { xray: { actors: true }, flash: hurtT > 0, alpha: hero.exposure === 0 ? .55 : 1 });\n513\t    for (const g of guards) { shadow(g); r.actor(g.x, g.y, g.z, (gg, ox, oy) => g.rig.draw(gg, ox, oy, r.view), { flash: g.stun > 0 && Math.floor(game.time * 10) % 2 === 0 }); }\n514\t    r.marker(ledger ? EXIT.x : LEDGER.x, ledger ? EXIT.y : LEDGER.y, ledger ? 0 : LEDGER.z, { label: ledger ? 'EAST GATE' : 'LEDGER', color: ledger ? '#80e0ff' : '#ffd040' });\n515\t    r.overlay(g => {\n516\t      for (const gd of guards) if (!gd.dead && gd.mind.state !== 'calm') {   // ? and ! over their heads, with the meter\n517\t        const [sx, sy] = r.w(gd.x, gd.y, gd.z + 46), a = gd.mind.state === 'alert';\n518\t        E.font.text(g, a ? '!' : '?', Math.round(sx), Math.round(sy) - 8, MOOD[gd.mind.state], { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n519\t        E.ui.bar(g, Math.round(sx) - 6, Math.round(sy) + 2, 12, 2, Math.min(1, gd.mind.level), MOOD[gd.mind.state]);\n520\t      }\n521\t    });\n522\t  }\n523\t  return { view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'], input: 'THIRDPERSON', res: 'ps1', pausable: true, touch: ['jump', 'attack', 'block', 'crouch'],\n524\t    camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], rotate: true }, enter: start, update, draw,\n525\t    state: () => ({ hero, guards, map, ledger, won, hp }),   // for tests\n526\t    /** the proof: over the rooftops, jumping, swinging and crouching, the guards on their rounds; a hash of the run */\n527\t    run: (n = 600) => proof('stealth', n, (i, k) => { walk(i, k, ['right', 'down', 'left', 'up'], 100); if (i % 130 === 60) k.tap('jump'); if (i % 90 === 45) k.tap('attack'); if (i === 400) k.tap('crouch'); },\n528\t      () => [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z, hp, ledger, won, guards.map(g => [g.x, g.y, g.z, g.hp, g.dead])]),\n529\t    exit() { game.cam.offset = null; L.enabled = false; if (ui) ui.hud({}); } };\n530\t})();\n531\tscenes.stealth = STEALTH;\n532\t\n533\t/* ---- START: the title menu, or a slice named in the address (#platformer) ---- */\n534\t// a genre kit file holds one slice: the menu lists only the slices in this file\n535\tfor (let i = SLICES.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (!scenes[SLICES[i].id]) SLICES.splice(i, 1);\n536\ttitleMenu = menuOf(SLICES, { y: 76, onPick: i => game.go(SLICES[i].id) });\n537\t// #<slice>/<part> jumps in (#arcade/maze, #shooter/horizontal): the slice's enter(data) gets { part }; a part that is a\n538\t// scene of its own (the slice's parts: { battle: 'rpg-battle' }) starts there\n539\tconst [first, part] = (location.hash || '').slice(1).split('/'), sc = scenes[first], to = sc && part && sc.parts && sc.parts[part];\n540\tgame.start({ scenes, scene: to || (sc ? first : 'title'), data: sc && part ? { part } : undefined });\n541\twindow.__game = { game, scenes, titleMenu };   // for tests\n542\t})();\n543\t/* =============================== GAME END =============================== */\n544\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2","uuid":"04cf1ba7-fe10-4ec5-8c6c-a4bf4885a46b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:24:04.769Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium--20261102-181322--x8b64cc-work/0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2/tool-results/bmdscsj46.txt","content":"// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n// end screens are pixel art.\n// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } } });   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\nconst ROOF = 32;\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['############',\n         '#..........#',\n         '#.@........#',\n         '#....p.....#',\n         '#......RRR.#',\n         '#......RGR.#',\n         '#..s...RRR.#',\n         '#..........#',\n         '############'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, R: 2, G: { tile: 2, spawn: 'gem' }, p: 3, '@': 'hero', s: 'guard' },\n  types: { 1: { h: 48, top: '#5a5068', side: '#3e3650', cut: true },\n           2: { h: ROOF, top: '#9a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n           3: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n  floorMat: 'cobble'   // a material (E.MATERIALS, or '#hex pattern'): the floor, wall faces and tops, shapes' parts all take them\n});\n// set dressing: shapes (E.SHAPES: objects as data, right in every view), solid where they stand (map.solid: walk into one, land on it)\nconst DRESS = [['barrel', 152, 30, { facing: .5 }], ['barrel', 166, 26, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 22, 120, { facing: .3 }], ['cart', 72, 26, { facing: 0 }]];\nfor (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) map.solid(id, x, y, 0, o);\nconst GEM = E.sprite(['.c.', 'cCc', '.c.'], { c: '#48c8f0', C: '#e8faff' }, 2);\nlet hero, heroRig, guard, guardRig, alert, got, won;\n\nfunction reset() {\n  const h = map.find('hero'), g = map.find('guard');\n  hero = new E.Mover({ x: h.x, y: h.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 24, glide: true, staminaMax: 100 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (the roof, 32 high, is climbed)\n  heroRig = heroRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hood: true, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth: '#3a4a6a', cape: '#2a3a52' } });\n  guard = new E.Body({ x: g.x, y: g.y, r: 5 }); guard.facing = 0; guard.dir = 1;\n  guardRig = guardRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'sword', hat: 'helmet', colors: { cloth: '#8a3a32' } });\n  alert = 0; got = false; won = false;\n}\n\nconst title = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(['#141030', '#3a2a60']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);   // centred on any screen\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'ROOFTOP', r.W / 2, m - 52, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('CLIMB WITH ' + game.input.label('jump') + '  TAKE THE GEM  STAY UNSEEN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 8, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center' });\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start')).toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 38, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nconst play = {\n  pausable: true,\n  enter() { game.follow(hero, { z: 16 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5; },\n  exit() { game.lights.enabled = false; ui.hud({}); },\n  update(dt) {\n    const I = game.input, was = !!(hero.wall || hero.action);\n    hero.update(dt, map, I);   // walks, jumps, climbs: the stick and the jump button, through the view\n    if (!was && (hero.wall || hero.action)) game.audio.sfx('jump');\n    // the guard walks the street and watches ahead: its eyes see over the planter, not through the roof\n    guard.vx = guard.dir * 30; guard.update(dt, map);\n    if (guard.x > 112 || guard.hitWall) guard.dir = -1; else if (guard.x < 40) guard.dir = 1;\n    guard.facing = guard.dir > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI;\n    const sees = map.sight(guard, hero) && E.inArc(guard, guard.facing, hero, 110, .6);\n    alert = sees ? alert + dt : Math.max(0, alert - dt * .5);\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got && E.dist(hero, { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }) < 12) { got = true; game.audio.sfx('coin'); game.flash('#c8f4ff', .15); }\n    if (got && hero.z < 2) { won = true; game.go('end'); }   // back down in the street with it\n    else if (alert > 1.2) { won = false; game.audio.sfx('hurt'); game.go('end'); }\n    // the rigs are posed every step from the bodies' motion; draw only draws them\n    heroRig.update(dt, hero.rigState());\n    guardRig.update(dt, { x: guard.x, y: guard.y, z: guard.z, vx: guard.vx, vy: 0, facing: guard.facing, stance: 'ready' });\n    // the HUD, from this step's state (E.Shell redraws only what changed; the keys hide on a touch screen)\n    ui.hud({ objective: got ? { title: 'Bring it down', text: 'Back to the street with it' } : { title: 'Take the gem', text: hero.wall ? 'Climb: up, and jump to leap' : 'It lies on the roof', at: { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }, from: hero },\n      bars: [{ label: 'Seen', value: Math.min(alert, 1.2), max: 1.2, color: '#ff6040' }, { label: 'Stamina', value: hero.stamina, max: hero.staminaMax, color: hero.exhausted ? '#ff6040' : '#7ad06a' }],\n      keys: [[['up', 'left', 'down', 'right'].map(a => I.label(a)).join(''), 'Move'], [I.label('jump'), 'Jump, climb, glide']] });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);   // (the floor runs on past the map to the screen's edges: map.outside)\n    for (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) r.shape(id, x, y, 0, o);\n    r.prop('lamp', 88, 88, 0, { light: true });   // a street lamp: its glow and a pool of light\n    r.decal(() => r.groundArc(guard.x, guard.y, 6, 110, guard.facing - .6, guard.facing + .6, alert > 0 ? '#ff6040' : '#ffe080', .4));   // its sight cone\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got) { r.sprite(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6 + Math.sin(game.time * 3) * 2, GEM, { glow: .8 }); game.lights.add(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6, 44, .9, { color: '#80d8ff' }); }\n    if (hero.gliding) r.queue(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 40, g => {   // the sail, over the hands the rig holds up\n      const c = Math.cos(hero.facing), s = Math.sin(hero.facing), P = (f, w, z) => r.w(hero.x + c * f - s * w, hero.y + s * f + c * w, hero.z + z);\n      const q = [P(9, -17, 43), P(9, 17, 43), P(-7, 15, 37), P(-7, -15, 37)], h = P(0, 0, 30);\n      for (const t of [q[0], q[1]]) E.px.line(g, t[0], t[1], h[0], h[1], '#3a2a20');\n      E.px.poly(g, q, '#d8603a'); E.px.line(g, q[0][0], q[0][1], q[1][0], q[1][1], '#f4a070');\n    });\n    for (const [b, rig] of [[hero, heroRig], [guard, guardRig]]) {\n      r.shadow(b.x, b.y, 7, .35, undefined, b.groundZ || 0);\n      r.actor(b.x, b.y, b.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst end = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(won ? ['#103020', '#2a6a48'] : ['#301010', '#6a2a2a']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, won ? 'STOLEN' : 'CAUGHT', r.W / 2, m - 42, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start') + ' TO TRY AGAIN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 28, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nreset();\n// a handle for tests and tools (node game/test.mjs, tools/check.mjs prints snapshot(), tools/replay.mjs logs it)\ngame.debug = {\n  snapshot: () => ({ scene: game.sceneName, hero: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z].map(v => Math.round(v * 10) / 10), climbing: !!(hero.wall || hero.action),\n    guard: [Math.round(guard.x), Math.round(guard.y), guard.facing], alert: Math.round(alert * 100) / 100, got, won }),\n  teleport(x, y, z = 0, facing = hero.facing) { Object.assign(hero, { x, y, z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, onGround: true, facing, wall: null, action: null }); }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { title, play, end }, scene: 'title' });\n})();\n// The STEALTH kit's game (third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/70-stealth.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. stealth.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs stealth runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\nconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {};\nlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\nconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n];\n/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\nconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n});\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\nconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\nconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\nconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n];\nHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\nconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\nconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\nconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n  try {\n    if (fresh) fresh();\n    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n    return h >>> 0;\n  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n};\n// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\nconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\nconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n    const t = game.time;\n    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n    });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n    titleBg.draw(r);\n    stage.draw(r);\n    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER: shared by every slice ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 118, onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? overMenu.from : 'title') });\nconst overBg = new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#12040c', '#3a0c1c', '#6a1a28'], moon: { x: .5, y: .3, r: 16, color: '#e8a0a0' }, stars: 30,\n  layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#2a0c16', y: .72, height: .3, parallax: 0 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a2a3a', y: .9, height: .12, parallax: 0, drift: 4 }] });\nscenes.over = {\n  view: 'side', input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter(d) { overMenu.from = d.from; overMenu.i = 0; A.music(null); A.sfx('die'); game.follow(null); game.focus(0, 0, 0); if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {   // centred on any screen\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 60; overMenu.y = y + 58;\n    overBg.draw(r); r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: '#3a0810' })); overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 7  STEALTH  (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu). A rooftop district at dusk: steal the ledger from the brick\n * roof and slip out by the east gate. Three guards (one on a roof) patrol with sight cones; what they see makes them\n * notice (?), search the last place they saw you, and at last chase (!) across the roofs. Hide in tall grass while\n * crouched, take a guard down silently from behind (J), or from a roof above (J as you stand over them). In a fight their\n * swings are telegraphed: K just before the blow parries and stuns them.\n * Keys (E.Input.THIRDPERSON): WASD move, Shift sprint, Space jump, climb a wall, vault, leap a gap, C crouch, J attack or\n * take down, K block or parry, L dodge roll, V view. The ledger is a checkpoint. The hero climbs any wall: Space at a\n * face latches on, the stick climbs (up the screen is up the wall), Space leaps up, C lets go. TOUCH: the stick, JUMP,\n * ATTACK, BLOCK, CROUCH.\n * HOW IT WORKS: the hero and the guards are E.Mover bodies (the same climbing, vaulting and gap-leaping for both); a\n * guard's eyes are E.sees through the map's heights, its mind an E.Suspicion, its legs a FlowField that climbs, drops and\n * jumps. Climbs, vaults, rolls and takedowns are E.ACTIONS; the facades are wall-type options; the belfry's canopy sorts by\n * its footprint; r.sightCone and r.marker draw the cones and the objective. Dusk is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n * ambient and the lights added each draw (street lamps, the ledger's glow, the gate), on a computer: its pass costs a\n * few milliseconds a frame, so a phone keeps its frame rate and an unlit street.\n * The interface is HTML, E.Shell's: the objective with its distance, health, status, the takedown prompt, toasts and\n * the results; the guards' marks stay in the world. The music is one song in layers (game.audio.layer): it sneaks on\n * three tracks, and a guard's alert brings in the chase's drums and its saw over them, taken out again when they lose\n * you: no cut to another song.\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst STEALTH = (() => {\n  const T = 16, HP = 3;\n  // SHADOWS ON THE ROOFS: the sneaking bass, ticks and lead; 'chase' and 'alarm' start silent (on: false)\n  const SONG = { bpm: 108, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: .28, notes: 'A2 . . A2 . . A2 . | A2 . . A2 . C3 . . | F2 . . F2 . . F2 . | G2 . . G2 . E2 . .' },\n    { name: 'tick', wave: 'drums', vol: .06, notes: 'h . . h . . h . h . . h . . h .' },\n    { name: 'lead', wave: 'pulse12', vol: .07, notes: 'E5 - . . . . D5 . | C5 - . . B4 . A4 . | . . . . F5 - E5 . | D5 - . . E5 - . . | E5 - . . . . G5 . | F5 - . . E5 . D5 . | C5 - . . D5 - . . | B4 - - - . . . .' },\n    { name: 'chase', wave: 'drums', vol: .13, on: false, notes: 'k . h k s . h . k k h . s . h s' },\n    { name: 'alarm', wave: 'saw', vol: .06, on: false, notes: 'A3 A3 A4 A3 E4 A3 G4 A3 | A3 A3 A4 A3 C5 A3 B4 A3 | F3 F3 F4 F3 C4 F3 E4 F3 | G3 G3 G4 G3 D4 G3 B3 G3' }] };\n  const PAVE = { stones: ['#7a6a60', '#726258', '#806e64'].map(E.hex), mortar: E.hex('#3e3236'), hi: E.hex('#8e7e72'), lo: E.hex('#56484a'), speck: E.hex('#66564e') };   // warm cobbles against the cool stone walls\n  /* ---- THE DISTRICT: roofs 24-56 high a jump apart (3-4 cells), a belfry, tall grass (,) and a planter (p) ---- */\n  const map = new E.TileMap({ rows: [\n    '############################',\n    '#.......................,,,#',\n    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC...,,#',\n    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC.....#',\n    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC..TT.#',\n    '#.AAAA...BBBBB....CCCC..TT.#',\n    '#.........................,#',\n    '#..,,,.......p.......,,,..,#',\n    '#..,,,...............,,,...#',\n    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF.......#',\n    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF..GGG..#',\n    '#.DDDD..EEE....FFFFF..GGG..#',\n    '#.@.......................X#',\n    '############################'],\n    legend: { '#': 1, A: 2, B: 3, C: 4, D: 5, E: 6, F: 7, G: 8, T: 9, p: 10, ',': { floor: 'grass' }, '@': 'hero', X: 'exit' },\n    types: {\n      1: { h: 64, top: '#3a3448', side: '#5a5068', face: 'stone', roof: 'plain', cut: true, cutH: 6 },   // the city wall drops low on the camera's side\n      2: { h: 40, top: '#8a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', windows: { lit: .3 }, shutters: '#2a5a8a', door: { chance: .4 } },\n      3: { h: 48, top: '#5a4a3a', side: '#9a6a4a', face: 'brick', roof: 'slab', windows: { lit: .2 }, balcony: { z: 30, color: '#3a2a1e' } },\n      4: { h: 40, top: '#4a6a3a', side: '#b8a888', face: 'timber', roof: 'tiles', arch: { chance: .5 }, windows: true },\n      5: { h: 24, top: '#7a4a32', side: '#d0c0a0', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', door: { chance: .5, color: '#5a2a1a' }, windows: { from: 12, lit: .4 } },\n      6: { h: 48, top: '#6a5a6a', side: '#7a7a8a', face: 'stone', roof: 'plain', windows: { w: 4, h: 12, lit: .15 } },\n      7: { h: 40, top: '#8a5a3a', side: '#c8a888', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles', windows: true, shutters: '#6a3a2a', balcony: { z: 24 } },\n      8: { h: 24, top: '#4a6a3a', side: '#a89878', face: 'timber', roof: 'tiles', arch: { chance: .6 } },\n      9: { h: 72, top: '#7a6a5a', side: '#a89878', face: 'sandstone', roof: 'plain', windows: { w: 3, h: 10, step: 22, lit: .5 } },   // the belfry: face, a MATERIAL (docs/ASSETS.md)\n      10: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n    floorTex: (x, y, tag) => tag === 'grass' ? E.tex.grass(x, y, { base: '#3e6a32', dark: '#2a5226', light: '#5a8a42' }) : E.tex.flagstone(x, y, PAVE)\n  });\n  const LEDGER = { x: 11.5 * T, y: 3.5 * T, z: 48 }, EXIT = map.find('exit'), GRASS = [];\n  // set dressing: SHAPES (E.SHAPES, docs/ASSETS.md: objects as data, right in every view) along the north street, out of the patrols' way\n  const DRESS = [['barrel', 1.5 * T, 1.4 * T, { facing: .4 }], ['barrel', 2.5 * T, 1.3 * T, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 7.4 * T, 1.4 * T, { scale: .8, facing: .2 }],\n    ['cart', 15.5 * T, 1.5 * T, { facing: 0 }], ['sack', 16.9 * T, 1.3 * T, { facing: 1 }], ['barrel', 22.6 * T, 1.4 * T, { facing: 3 }],\n    // stacked planks from the asset store, cut into the page's 'stealth' set (src/assets/sets/stealth.js; none without it)\n    ...(E.addAssets((window.ASSETS || {}).stealth || { set: 'stealth' }).shapes.length ? [['stealth:resource-planks', 12.2 * T, 1.4 * T, { scale: .7, facing: Math.PI / 2 + .1 }]] : [])];\n  for (let cy = 0; cy < map.h; cy++) for (let cx = 0; cx < map.w; cx++) if (map.floorAt((cx + .5) * T, (cy + .5) * T) === 'grass') GRASS.push([(cx + .5) * T, (cy + .5) * T]);\n  const BOOK = E.sprite(['.bbbb.', 'bBBBBb', 'bBwwBb', 'bBBBBb', '.bbbb.'], { b: '#3a2010', B: '#8a3a20', w: '#f0e0b0' });\n  const ROUTES = [   // [start, ...patrol points] in cells, and the guard's roof height\n    [[19.5, 3.5, 40], [21.5, 3.5, 40], [21.5, 5.5, 40], [18.5, 5.5, 40]],\n    [[6.5, 6.5, 0], [20.5, 6.5, 0], [20.5, 8.5, 0], [6.5, 8.5, 0]],\n    [[11.5, 12.2, 0], [20.5, 12.2, 0], [20.5, 8.2, 0], [11.5, 8.2, 0]]\n  ];\n  let hero, rig, guards, attack, checkpoint, ledger, won, over, hp, hurtT, alertT, ui = null;\n  const say = (title, text) => ui.toast(title, text, 3);\n  const inGrass = b => b.z < 2 && map.floorAt(b.x, b.y) === 'grass';\n\n  /* ---- GUARDS: a Mover with patrol points, eyes, a mind and a flow field that climbs, drops and jumps ---- */\n  function makeGuard(route, i) {\n    const [x, y, z] = route[0];\n    const g = new E.Mover({ x: x * T, y: y * T, z, r: 5, run: 70, walk: 30, climbMax: 56, hopMax: 56 });\n    Object.assign(g, { i, route: route.map(p => [p[0] * T, p[1] * T]), at: 1, mind: new E.Suspicion({ rise: 1.6, decay: .25, forget: 7 }), hp: 2, stun: 0, dead: false,\n      flow: new E.FlowField(map, { climb: 56, drop: 56, jump: 60 }), wait: 0, hit: null, swing: new E.Attack('overhead', { wind: .38, recover: .3, reach: 9 }), bark: 0,\n      rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', hat: 'helmet', armor: true, weapon: 'sword', colors: { cloth: ['#8a3a32', '#6a3a5a', '#7a4a2a'][i], metal: '#c8c8d8' } }) });\n    return g;\n  }\n  function guardUpdate(g, dt) {\n    if (g.dead) return;   // (a takedown moves the body it takes: the hero's action plays it)\n    if (g.stun > 0) { g.stun -= dt; g.update(dt, map, { move: [0, 0] }); return; }\n    const seen = hero && !over ? E.sees(g, hero, { map, range: 110, fov: 1.5 }) : { seen: false, exposure: 0 }, st = g.mind.update(dt, seen, hero);\n    if (g.mind.changed && st === 'alert') { A.sfx('select'); g.bark = 1.2; }\n    let goal = null, speed = 'walk';\n    if (st === 'alert') { goal = hero; speed = 'run'; }\n    else if (st === 'search' && g.mind.last) goal = g.mind.last;\n    else if (st === 'notice') { g.facing = E.approachAng(g.facing, Math.atan2(g.mind.last.y - g.y, g.mind.last.x - g.x), dt * 3); g.update(dt, map, { move: [0, 0] }); return; }\n    else { const p = g.route[g.at]; goal = { x: p[0], y: p[1], z: 0 }; if (Math.hypot(p[0] - g.x, p[1] - g.y) < 8) { g.at = (g.at + 1) % g.route.length; g.wait = .8; } }\n    if (g.wait > 0 && st === 'calm') { g.wait -= dt; g.update(dt, map, { move: [0, 0] }); return; }\n    // in reach of the hero: a telegraphed swing (a long wind-up), else walk the field toward the goal\n    const d = Math.hypot(hero.x - g.x, hero.y - g.y), near = st === 'alert' && d < 20 && E.sameLevel(g, hero, 10);\n    if (near && !g.swing.busy && !hero.action) { g.facing = Math.atan2(hero.y - g.y, hero.x - g.x); g.swing.start(); A.sfx('swing', { vol: .5 }); }\n    const began = g.swing.update(dt);\n    if (g.swing.busy) { g.update(dt, map, { move: [0, 0] }); if (g.swing.active && began === 'active') strikeHero(g); return; }\n    let move = [0, 0], jump = false;\n    if (goal) {\n      g.flow.update(goal.x, goal.y);\n      const nx = g.flow.next(g.x, g.y), tx = nx ? nx.x : goal.x, ty = nx ? nx.y : goal.y, l = Math.hypot(tx - g.x, ty - g.y) || 1;\n      if (Math.hypot(goal.x - g.x, goal.y - g.y) > 6) move = [(tx - g.x) / l, (ty - g.y) / l];\n      if (nx && g.onGround && (nx.kind === 'climb' || nx.kind === 'jump') && nx.edge < g.r + 4) { jump = true; g.facing = Math.atan2(ty - g.y, tx - g.x); }\n    }\n    if (speed === 'walk') move = move.map(v => v * .5);\n    g.update(dt, map, { move, sprint: false, jumpPressed: jump });\n  }\n  function strikeHero(g) {\n    if (!E.inArc(g, g.facing, hero, 20, 1.2, 10) || (hero.action && hero.action.invulnerable)) return;\n    if (game.input.down('block') && !hero.action) { A.sfx('hit', { vol: .4 }); P.sparks(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 16, 6, g.facing + Math.PI); return; }\n    hp--; hurtT = .4; game.hitFx(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 16, { power: 1, angle: g.facing, sound: 'hurt' }); E.knockback(g, hero, 140);\n    if (hp <= 0) lose();\n  }\n\n  /* ---- THE HERO: a Mover, a hidden blade, a parry, two takedowns ---- */\n  function start() {\n    const s = map.find('hero');\n    hero = new E.Mover({ x: s.x, y: s.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 30 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (walls up to 30 are pulled up at once, higher ones climbed)\n    rig = rig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', hood: true, weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 7, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.4 }, colors: { cloth: '#d8d2c4', coat: '#d8d2c4', cape: '#8a2a2a', capeIn: '#5a1a1a', pants: '#3a3448', metal: '#e8e8f0' } });\n    attack = new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }); guards = ROUTES.map(makeGuard);\n    ui = ui || new E.Shell(game, { theme: { accent: '#e8c070' } });   // (made once: it takes over from the engine's own, keeping the pause menu)\n    checkpoint = null; ledger = false; won = false; over = false; hp = HP; hurtT = 0; alertT = 0; say('Steal the ledger', 'It lies on the brick roof');\n    game.follow(hero, { z: 18 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.cam.offset = [0, -10]; L.enabled = !!(window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(pointer: fine)').matches); L.ambient = .6; A.music(SONG); A.layer('chase', 0, .02); A.layer('alarm', 0, .02);\n  }\n  function respawnAt(cp) {\n    Object.assign(hero, { x: cp.x, y: cp.y, z: cp.z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, onGround: true, action: null }); hp = HP;\n    guards.forEach((g, i) => { if (!g.dead) { const [x, y, z] = ROUTES[i][0]; Object.assign(g, { x: x * T, y: y * T, z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, at: 1, stun: 0, action: null }); g.mind.reset(); g.swing.cancel(); } });\n    game.cam.snap = true; say('Back at the checkpoint');\n  }\n  function lose() { if (checkpoint) { A.sfx('die'); respawnAt(checkpoint); } else { over = true; game.after(.8, () => game.go('over', { from: 'stealth' })); } }\n  // a takedown within reach: [guard, from above] or null\n  function takedown() {\n    for (const g of guards) {\n      if (g.dead || g.action) continue;\n      const dz = hero.z - g.z, d = Math.hypot(g.x - hero.x, g.y - hero.y);\n      // from above: the hero stands over a guard below, close enough to drop onto them\n      if (dz > 14 && d < 44 && hero.onGround) return [g, true];\n      // from behind: close, on the same level, outside the guard's view and not yet hunting\n      const behind = Math.abs(E.angDiff(g.facing, Math.atan2(g.y - hero.y, g.x - hero.x))) < 1.1;\n      if (E.sameLevel(hero, g) && d < 18 && behind && g.mind.state !== 'alert') return [g, false];\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n  function tryTakedown() { const t = takedown(); if (!t) return false; hero.play('takedown', { other: t[0], aerial: t[1], map }); return finishGuard(t[0], hero.action); }\n  const parrying = () => guards.some(g => !g.dead && g.swing.phase === 'wind' && g.swing.u > .35 && Math.hypot(g.x - hero.x, g.y - hero.y) < 26);\n  function finishGuard(g, act) { g.dead = true; g.action = act; A.sfx('punch'); game.freeze(.06); return true; }\n  function heroUpdate(dt) {\n    const I = game.input;\n    hero.exposure = inGrass(hero) && hero.crouch ? 0 : 1;   // crouched in tall grass: unseen\n    if (!hero.action) {\n      if (I.pressed('dodge') && hero.dodge(undefined, 34)) A.sfx('whoosh');\n      else if (I.pressed('attack') && !tryTakedown() && attack.start()) { I.consume('attack'); A.sfx('swing'); }\n    }\n    attack.update(dt);\n    attack.hits(guards.filter(g => !g.dead), g => E.inArc(hero, hero.facing, g, 20, 1.3, 10), g => {\n      game.hitFx(g.x, g.y, g.z + 16, { power: g.stun > 0 ? 2 : 1, angle: hero.facing }); E.knockback(hero, g, 90);\n      if (g.stun > 0 || --g.hp <= 0) { g.dead = true; g.action = null; A.sfx('die', { vol: .5 }); } else g.mind.level = 1.2;\n    });\n    // a parry: block in the last moments of a guard's wind-up\n    // CONTEXT touch buttons: ATTACK says TAKE DOWN when one is in reach, BLOCK says PARRY in a guard's wind-up\n    I.touchSet('attack', !hero.action && takedown() ? 'TAKE DOWN' : null); I.touchSet('block', parrying() ? 'PARRY' : null);\n    if (I.pressed('block')) for (const g of guards) if (!g.dead && g.swing.phase === 'wind' && g.swing.u > .35 && Math.hypot(g.x - hero.x, g.y - hero.y) < 26) {\n      g.swing.cancel(); g.stun = 1.3; A.sfx('kick'); game.flash('#ffffff', .08); P.sparks(g.x, g.y, g.z + 18, 10, hero.facing); say('Parried');\n    }\n    hero.update(dt, map, attack.busy ? { move: [0, 0] } : I);\n    if (hero.hurt) { hp--; hurtT = .4; game.shake(3); if (hp <= 0) lose(); }\n    if (hero.inHazard) hero.respawn();\n    if (!ledger && E.dist(hero, LEDGER) < 12) { ledger = true; checkpoint = { x: hero.x, y: hero.y, z: hero.z }; A.sfx('powerup'); say('Checkpoint', 'The ledger is yours: now the east gate'); }\n    if (ledger && !won && Math.hypot(hero.x - EXIT.x, hero.y - EXIT.y) < 14 && hero.z < 2) { won = true; A.music('victory'); results(); }\n  }\n\n  function results() {\n    const alive = guards.filter(g => !g.dead).length, top = best('stealth', alive);\n    ui.show('results', { kicker: 'Mission complete', title: 'The ledger is out', stats: [[String(alive), 'guards who never fell'], [String(top), 'the best yet'], [String(HP - hp), 'wounds taken']],\n      actions: [{ label: 'Back to the title', primary: true, fn: () => { ui.hide(); game.go('title'); } }] });\n  }\n  // the HUD, from this step's state: E.Shell redraws only what changed (keys hide by themselves on a touch screen)\n  function hud() {\n    const k = a => game.input.label(a).toUpperCase(), pad = game.input.lastDevice === 'gamepad', td = !hero.action && takedown();\n    ui.hud(won || over ? {} : {\n      objective: ledger ? { step: '02 / 02', title: 'Slip out by the east gate', text: 'Down in the street, at the far end', at: { x: EXIT.x, y: EXIT.y, z: 0 }, from: hero }\n        : { step: '01 / 02', title: 'Steal the ledger', text: 'On the brick roof', at: LEDGER, from: hero },\n      status: hero.exposure === 0 ? { text: 'Hidden', color: '#9ae89a' } : alertT > 0 ? { text: 'Hunted', color: '#ff4a3a' } : hero.crouch ? 'Crouched' : null,\n      bars: [{ label: 'Health', value: hp, max: HP, kind: 'pips', color: '#e8505a' }], counts: [['Guards down', guards.filter(g => g.dead).length]],\n      prompt: touch() ? null : td ? { act: 'attack', label: 'Take down', hint: td[1] ? 'From above' : 'From behind' } : parrying() ? { act: 'block', label: 'Parry' } : null,\n      keys: [[pad ? 'STICK' : ['up', 'left', 'down', 'right'].map(k).join(''), 'Move'], [k('sprint'), 'Sprint'], [k('jump'), 'Jump, climb'], [k('crouch'), 'Crouch'], [k('attack'), 'Strike'], [k('block'), 'Block'], [k('dodge'), 'Roll']]\n    });\n  }\n\n  function update(dt) {\n    if (hurtT > 0) hurtT -= dt;\n    if (won || over) { hud(); rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ pose: won ? 'cheer' : null })); return; }\n    heroUpdate(dt);\n    for (const g of guards) guardUpdate(g, dt);\n    const alert = guards.some(g => !g.dead && g.mind.state === 'alert');\n    if (alert !== alertT > 0) { alertT = alert ? 1 : 0; A.layer('chase', alert ? 1 : 0, alert ? .4 : 2.5); A.layer('alarm', alert ? 1 : 0, alert ? .8 : 2.5); }   // (the chase comes in by layers, and fades out)\n    rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack: attack.state, pose: game.input.down('block') && !hero.action ? 'block' : null, hurt: hurtT > 0 }));\n    for (const g of guards) {\n      if (g.dead) { g.rig.update(dt, g.action && g.action.other === g ? g.action.otherState() : { x: g.x, y: g.y, z: g.z, facing: g.facing, down: 1 }); continue; }\n      g.rig.update(dt, g.rigState({ attack: g.swing.state, stance: g.mind.state === 'alert' ? 'ready' : null, hurt: g.stun > 0 }));\n      if (g.bark > 0) g.bark -= dt;\n    }\n    hud();\n  }\n\n  const MOOD = { calm: '#ffe080', notice: '#ffc040', search: '#ff9a40', alert: '#ff4a3a' };\n  const LAMPS = [[8.5, 6.2], [16, 8.8], [23.5, 6.2], [12.5, 10.5], [19.5, 1.3]].map(([x, y]) => [x * T, y * T]);   // street lamps, clear of the patrols\n  function draw(r) {\n    map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);   // (the street runs on past the walls to the screen's edges: map.outside)\n    for (const [x, y] of GRASS) r.prop('grass', x, y, 0, { size: 1.3 });\n    for (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) r.shape(id, x, y, 0, o);\n    for (const [x, y] of LAMPS) r.prop('lamp', x, y, 0, { light: true });   // each glows and lights the street (game.lights)\n    if (!ledger) L.add(LEDGER.x, LEDGER.y, LEDGER.z + 6, 40, .8, { color: '#ffd060' }); else L.add(EXIT.x, EXIT.y, 12, 56, .9, { color: '#80e0ff' });\n    // the belfry: a canopy wider than the tower, sorted by its whole footprint (over every tower block)\n    const bx = 25 * T, by = 5 * T, w = 21, H = 20, z = 72;\n    r.queue(bx, by, z, g => { const P2 = (x, y, zz) => r.w(x, y, zz), c = [P2(bx - w, by - w, z), P2(bx + w, by - w, z), P2(bx + w, by + w, z), P2(bx - w, by + w, z)], tip = P2(bx, by, z + H);\n      for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) px.poly(g, [c[i], c[(i + 1) % 4], tip], ['#7a3a2a', '#9a4a32', '#6a2a22', '#8a4232'][i]);\n      px.line(g, tip[0], tip[1], tip[0], tip[1] - 6, '#e8c860'); }, { footprint: [bx - w, by - w, bx + w, by + w] });\n    for (const g of guards) if (!g.dead) r.sightCone(g, { map, range: 110, fov: 1.5, color: MOOD[g.mind.state], alpha: g.mind.state === 'calm' ? .22 : .38 });\n    if (!ledger) r.sprite(LEDGER.x, LEDGER.y, LEDGER.z + 4 + Math.sin(game.time * 3) * 1.5, BOOK, { glow: .6 });\n    const shadow = b => r.shadow(b.x, b.y, 6, .35, undefined, map.groundAt(b.x, b.y, b.r, b.z));\n    shadow(hero); r.actor(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view), { xray: { actors: true }, flash: hurtT > 0, alpha: hero.exposure === 0 ? .55 : 1 });\n    for (const g of guards) { shadow(g); r.actor(g.x, g.y, g.z, (gg, ox, oy) => g.rig.draw(gg, ox, oy, r.view), { flash: g.stun > 0 && Math.floor(game.time * 10) % 2 === 0 }); }\n    r.marker(ledger ? EXIT.x : LEDGER.x, ledger ? EXIT.y : LEDGER.y, ledger ? 0 : LEDGER.z, { label: ledger ? 'EAST GATE' : 'LEDGER', color: ledger ? '#80e0ff' : '#ffd040' });\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      for (const gd of guards) if (!gd.dead && gd.mind.state !== 'calm') {   // ? and ! over their heads, with the meter\n        const [sx, sy] = r.w(gd.x, gd.y, gd.z + 46), a = gd.mind.state === 'alert';\n        E.font.text(g, a ? '!' : '?', Math.round(sx), Math.round(sy) - 8, MOOD[gd.mind.state], { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n        E.ui.bar(g, Math.round(sx) - 6, Math.round(sy) + 2, 12, 2, Math.min(1, gd.mind.level), MOOD[gd.mind.state]);\n      }\n    });\n  }\n  return { view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'], input: 'THIRDPERSON', res: 'ps1', pausable: true, touch: ['jump', 'attack', 'block', 'crouch'],\n    camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], rotate: true }, enter: start, update, draw,\n    state: () => ({ hero, guards, map, ledger, won, hp }),   // for tests\n    /** the proof: over the rooftops, jumping, swinging and crouching, the guards on their rounds; a hash of the run */\n    run: (n = 600) => proof('stealth', n, (i, k) => { walk(i, k, ['right', 'down', 'left', 'up'], 100); if (i % 130 === 60) k.tap('jump'); if (i % 90 === 45) k.tap('attack'); if (i === 400) k.tap('crouch'); },\n      () => [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z, hp, ledger, won, guards.map(g => [g.x, g.y, g.z, g.hp, g.dead])]),\n    exit() { game.cam.offset = null; L.enabled = false; if (ui) ui.hud({}); } };\n})();\nscenes.stealth = STEALTH;\n\n/* ---- START: the title menu, or a slice named in the address (#platformer) ---- */\n// a genre kit file holds one slice: the menu lists only the slices in this file\nfor (let i = SLICES.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (!scenes[SLICES[i].id]) SLICES.splice(i, 1);\ntitleMenu = menuOf(SLICES, { y: 76, onPick: i => game.go(SLICES[i].id) });\n// #<slice>/<part> jumps in (#arcade/maze, #shooter/horizontal): the slice's enter(data) gets { part }; a part that is a\n// scene of its own (the slice's parts: { battle: 'rpg-battle' }) starts there\nconst [first, part] = (location.hash || '').slice(1).split('/'), sc = scenes[first], to = sc && part && sc.parts && sc.parts[part];\ngame.start({ scenes, scene: to || (sc ? first : 'title'), data: sc && part ? { part } : undefined });\nwindow.__game = { game, scenes, titleMenu };   // for tests\n})();\n/* =============================== GAME END =============================== */\n","numLines":544,"startLine":1,"totalLines":544}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01M9WRwADHciorWc91jBiLrx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
