{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHvu4wuawhg2mA4qzYtidT","type":"tool_result","content":"471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus \n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jum\n822:- `flow.update(x, y)`: aim the field at a world point; it rebuilds only when the target's cell or the map (map.version) changes\n823:- `flow.climb`: how much higher a next-door top may be (an agent that climbs walls)\n824:- `flow.d`: each cell's distance in steps to the target cell (1e9 where it can't get there), row by row\n825:- `flow.drop`: how much lower (an agent that hops down)\n826:- `flow.jump` †: the widest gap jumped (world units, 0 = none)\n827:- `flow.jumpDrop`, `flow.jumpRise` †: how much higher and lower a jump may land\n828:- `flow.map`: the map it paths over\n829:- `flow.step`: the height difference walked over freely (2)\n830:- `flow.tx = -1`, `flow.ty = -1`: the target's cell\n831:- `flow.version = -1`: the map's version it was built for\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1004:- `suspicion.reset()` †: back to calm\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1006:- `suspicion.alert = 1`, `suspicion.notice = .3`, `suspicion.search = .65` †: the levels where each state starts\n1007:- `suspicion.changed = false` †: the state changed this step\n1008:- `suspicion.decay = .3`, `suspicion.rise = 1.5` †: per second\n1009:- `suspicion.forget = 6` †: seconds an alert guard searches after losing the target\n1010:- `suspicion.last = null` †: where it last saw or heard the target ({ x, y, z }), or null\n1011:- `suspicion.level = 0` †: 0..1.2, how suspicious\n1012:- `suspicion.since = 0` †: seconds since it last saw or heard anything\n1013:- `suspicion.state = 'calm'` †: 'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'\n1019:- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n1020:- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n1021:- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n1022:- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n1025:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1026:- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n1027:- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n1028:- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n1029:- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181322__x8b64cc/work\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: BreakingBond-BreakingBad-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181322/src/10-world.js. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7f9d2-08b6-4da9-9a1b-3a3d42ba1fc2","uuid":"64700c1d-23f9-4331-918c-e72fce641467","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:32:37.033Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus \n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jum\n822:- `flow.update(x, y)`: aim the field at a world point; it rebuilds only when the target's cell or the map (map.version) changes\n823:- `flow.climb`: how much higher a next-door top may be (an agent that climbs walls)\n824:- `flow.d`: each cell's distance in steps to the target cell (1e9 where it can't get there), row by row\n825:- `flow.drop`: how much lower (an agent that hops down)\n826:- `flow.jump` †: the widest gap jumped (world units, 0 = none)\n827:- `flow.jumpDrop`, `flow.jumpRise` †: how much higher and lower a jump may land\n828:- `flow.map`: the map it paths over\n829:- `flow.step`: the height difference walked over freely (2)\n830:- `flow.tx = -1`, `flow.ty = -1`: the target's cell\n831:- `flow.version = -1`: the map's version it was built for\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1004:- `suspicion.reset()` †: back to calm\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1006:- `suspicion.alert = 1`, `suspicion.notice = .3`, `suspicion.search = .65` †: the levels where each state starts\n1007:- `suspicion.changed = false` †: the state changed this step\n1008:- `suspicion.decay = .3`, `suspicion.rise = 1.5` †: per second\n1009:- `suspicion.forget = 6` †: seconds an alert guard searches after losing the target\n1010:- `suspicion.last = null` †: where it last saw or heard the target ({ x, y, z }), or null\n1011:- `suspicion.level = 0` †: 0..1.2, how suspicious\n1012:- `suspicion.since = 0` †: seconds since it last saw or heard anything\n1013:- `suspicion.state = 'calm'` †: 'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'\n1019:- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n1020:- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n1021:- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n1022:- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n1025:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1026:- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n1027:- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n1028:- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n1029:- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181322__x8b64cc/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: BreakingBond-BreakingBad-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181322/src/10-world.js. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181322__x8b64cc/work/BreakingBond-BreakingBad-claude-opus-5-5-medium-2026110